{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil","id":217641,"title":"The Lie and The Vigil","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-03T16:57:20-07:00","id":217641,"title":"The Lie and The Vigil","content":"Disclaimer: I've only recently started taking an interest in Mage, since we started getting teasers about The Fallen World Chronicle. Sorry if what seems like a revelation to me is already old hat to longtime Mage fans.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I've been thinking about Hunters lately and what exactly their relationship is with The Lie. There was some discussion in the weekly blog thread about it, and whether or not Hunters should count a sleepwalkers. There is definitely a lot of grey area, and that seems very much appropriate to the themes of Hunter, which asks at what point a well-intentioned human becomes the very monster they hunt. But here's where my own musings on the subject have lead me to.<br /> <br /> Setting aside the conspiracies like the Lucifuge that <i>really</i> toe the line between mortal and monster, at their core a Hunter is just a mortal who has had an encounter with the supernatural, and rather than rationalizing or dismissing it like other Sleepers would, they actually learn from the encounter. Mechanically, this takes the form of Practical Experience, and it demonstrates that Hunters must be seeing past the lie on <i>some level,</i> and on the surface, sure, it does look an awful lot like sleepwalking. But maybe there's something else going on - something far more sinister. To paraphrase Morpheus, many of these people are not yet ready to be Awakened. And many of them are so inured, so hopelessly dependent on The Lie, that they will fight to protect it. And maybe that's what Hunters really are - people who have been faced with something so overtly supernatural that they can't simply ignore it, but instead of seeing beyond The Lie, they take up arms to protect it from the things they believe should not be.<br /> <br /> So here's where I get a little speculative. What if, when a Hunter first has that eye-opening experience, The Lie is no longer able to maintain the illusion of a sublunary world, so in order to keep them in control, it begins to affect them in a different way. The blissfully ignorant dream of such a sleeper turns into a nightmare. Rather than distorting the memory of a supernatural encounter into something mundane and explainable, it distorts it into something even more horrifying; it pushes the Hunter to fear the supernatural rather than simply ignore it. One feature of this explanation that makes it particularly appealing to me is that it creates an <i>in universe</i> explanation for why monsters use different rules in Hunter than they do their respective game lines. It's not simply that the Hunters don't fully understand what they're encountering - though that is part of it - it's also that their memory of their encounters with those monsters is actually being altered by The Lie. If you want to go even deeper with it, maybe Practical Experience is a direct result of this distortion. The Lie is actively aiding the Hunters in fighting against the supernatural; empowering the few who manage to see beyond it in their fight to keep the rest of the Sleepers believing themselves to be disempowered.<br /> <br /> So yeah, that's what's been on my mind, and I'd be interested to hear others' takes on it. Is this an interesting new idea, or something that's already been thoroughly explored? What implications might this take on The Vigil as a product of The Lie have on Mage and/or Hunter games? Any ideas on how to expand or improve on the concept?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T18:06:45-07:00","id":217704,"title":"","content":"My one qualm with the notion of hunters as pawns of the Lie is that it runs counter to the \u201clights in the darkness\u201d theme. I <i>do</i> think that it\u2019s the sort of theory that a mage who has ended up on the receiving end of a witch hunt might concoct; and it <i>does</i> hold together fairly well. Perhaps a more positive spin on it might be to find and play up any positive aspects of the Lie that might exist. There aren\u2019t many, especially once you take Supernal magic out of the picture (the Lie doesn\u2019t cause other supernatural phenomena to unravel or to suffer anything like Paradox Risk); in fact, I can\u2019t think of any off the top of my head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T18:17:14-07:00","id":217709,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I agree it kills the hopeful aspect of Hunter. I probably would not employ this interpretation in a Hunter game unless I wanted to tell a downer &quot;you were the bad guy all along&quot; story... And not a lot of people actually want to play that kind of game. But it works well if you want to use Hunters as antagonists in a Mage game, I think. The theory is definitely from the perspective of a Mage, going along with the idea that Mages like to try to fit everything within their worldview. It could well be that this is how a Mage would understand the tendency of Hunters who should by all rights be Sleepers somehow learning from each encounter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-03-2014, 09:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T18:56:37-07:00","id":217758,"title":"","content":"The \u201cofficial\u201d answer for this appears to be \u201cif you want hunters in your <b>Mage</b> game, use Banishers\u201d. But yeah; if I was running a \u201cdon\u2019t underestimate Sleepers\u201d storyline, something along these lines would make sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T20:46:46-07:00","id":217851,"title":"","content":"I'm probably not going to use the Lie except as a background element to indicate that most people have odd explanations for actions of high level witches. <br /> For simplicity, I'll use Witchfinders instead of Mage for my Hunter game, but I may change my mind after I've read the Sleeper section of FWC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T21:30:40-07:00","id":217870,"title":"","content":"Personally, I\u2019d be more inclined to use the sorcerers in <b>Mortal Remains</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T21:31:44-07:00","id":217872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=217704#post217704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My one qualm with the notion of hunters as pawns of the Lie is that it runs counter to the \u201clights in the darkness\u201d theme. I <i>do</i> think that it\u2019s the sort of theory that a mage who has ended up on the receiving end of a witch hunt might concoct; and it <i>does</i> hold together fairly well..</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda agrees with my notion a bit. Mine is tends to be that Hunters start emerging if one starts being a dick/gets too reckless. The idea that the Lie is actively recruiting sleepers to hunt Mages is great as an in-game excuse that Mages tell themselves to help go to the sleep at night. <br /> <br /> But the truth is a bit more simpler. They are mostly after you because you fucked up and most likely killed someone they hold dear. Keywords being &quot;Fucked up&quot; and &quot;Killed&quot;.<br /> <br /> It keeps human agency for Hunters and leans very well to the hubris of Mage.<br /> <br /> Mage: &quot;Oh those Sleepers are pawns of the Lie. Of Course they're after us! They can't help themselves!&quot;<br /> <br /> Hunter: &quot;You fucked up your spell which went out of control and lead to a school bus crashing, killing my son and his other 15 classmates.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T23:08:18-07:00","id":217897,"title":"","content":"Maybe the act of seeing the supernatural and refusing the Lie is possible if you have the sheer stubborn Will to do so? I mean, Hunters are the only ones who can risk Willpower for a reason. Hunters haven't woken up, they've become sleepwalkers from sheer force of Will. I like the idea of Practical experience being the way Hunters cope and learn from what was already right in front of them, but now they can actually <i>see</i> it..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T23:11:35-07:00","id":217899,"title":"","content":"Do you also remove Lunacy when your hunters are up against werewolves?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":14,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","user":"Dave Brookshaw","date":".  EDIT - Lunacy, even! 08-04-2014, 05:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T23:18:52-07:00","id":217906,"title":"","content":"Most of the time, yes. I'm a huge advocate for the players being special cases. That's not to say I don't play with my descriptions, and mess with the perception of the scene. There is always an effect, but I hate feeling like I'm taking away a player's ability to act.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T23:34:36-07:00","id":217915,"title":"","content":"Conversely, a good case could be made that the whole point of <b>Hunter: the Vigil</b> is precisely that they\u2019re <i>not</i> special cases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T02:08:18-07:00","id":217979,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Remembering what happened clearly when you witnessed magic is called <i>being a Sleepwalker</i>. If you want your Hunter characters to have that, give them the Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T03:50:22-07:00","id":218003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=217872#post217872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kinda agrees with my notion a bit. Mine is tends to be that Hunters start emerging if one starts being a dick/gets too reckless. The idea that the Lie is actively recruiting sleepers to hunt Mages is great as an in-game excuse that Mages tell themselves to help go to the sleep at night.<br /> <br /> But the truth is a bit more simpler. They are mostly after you because you fucked up and most likely killed someone they hold dear. Keywords being &quot;Fucked up&quot; and &quot;Killed&quot;.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's already in the game though, you don't need to give Hunters any super special lie beating powers for that.<br /> <br /> Hunter: &quot;You fucked me up, so I used the Beats I got from that Breaking Point to buy the Sleepwalker merit. Now I'm gonna fuck <i>you</i> up.<br /> <br /> You could make a houserule that any time a Sleeper suffers a breaking point from supernal magic they reduce the price of the Sleepwalker merit by one Beat, down to a minimum of one, on top of the beats they get from the breaking point anyway. That way you still have sleepers that never begin to sleepwalk, and doing magic in front of sleepers significantly increases the risk of Sleepwalker Hunters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","user":"Joker","date":". 08-04-2014, 06:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T03:53:02-07:00","id":218004,"title":"","content":"Dave, I wasn't advocating against the merit, I was simply responding the the theory crafting going on. A way of looking at hunters positively, as opposed to unknowing pawns of the Lie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T04:38:34-07:00","id":218026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=218004#post218004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dave, I wasn't advocating against the merit, I was simply responding the the theory crafting going on. A way of looking at hunters positively, as opposed to unknowing pawns of the Lie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunters aren't magical, not explicitly. They aren't all-knowing and they don't know what's good and what's bad. Having them be these special people who know when somethings wrong isn't the type of hunter the books have been writing about. Which is fine. You can change the way your hunters work but the default is hunters go in blind and they generally have no clue what's good or bad unless they get lucky. In most cases, that probably still wouldn't change their outlook on non-human beings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T09:03:39-07:00","id":218231,"title":"","content":"I'm compromising a bit. I'm using Hunter Core along with Mortal Remains (with its GMC update) and Witchfinders, so I'll use the rules contained therein for Integrity (and Lunacy), but since the Quiescent Curse is only mentioned in a sidebar for players using the Mage: the Awakening Core, and is not given mechanics, I'll wait until FWC comes out so I can read over the Sleeper section before I decide whether to add the amnesia aspects of the Lie into my Hunter game. For gnosis 5 witches, I'll use the simplified rules for paradox in Witchfinders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T09:10:33-07:00","id":218238,"title":"","content":"The Quiescent Curse absolutely has game mechanics in the current edition of Mage - look for &quot;Disbelief&quot; in the Paradox section, and find a table of Willpower dot scores and how much they mean the character forgets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T09:16:55-07:00","id":218243,"title":"","content":"I think Octavo meant in <i>Witchfinders </i>for HtV, not the MtAw Core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T09:28:03-07:00","id":218252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=218238#post218238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Quiescent Curse absolutely has game mechanics in the current edition of Mage - look for &quot;Disbelief&quot; in the Paradox section, and find a table of Willpower dot scores and how much they mean the character forgets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Saibot is correct. I'm trying to say that I'm not mixing any current edition Mage into my Hunter game, but I'm open to mixing future Mage (Fallen World Chronicle) into my current or future Hunter games. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":61,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","user":"Octavo","date":". 08-04-2014, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T10:37:10-07:00","id":218350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=217979#post217979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. Remembering what happened clearly when you witnessed magic is called <i>being a Sleepwalker</i>. If you want your Hunter characters to have that, give them the Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. The point of my idea was specifically so that Hunters don't remember <i>clearly</i> that they witnessed magic, but they don't write it off as not magic either. Also, to give Hunters a bit of a darker, more tragic spin in the context of Mage games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T10:39:04-07:00","id":218352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=218004#post218004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dave, I wasn't advocating against the merit, I was simply responding the the theory crafting going on. A way of looking at hunters positively, as opposed to unknowing pawns of the Lie.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the way to look at Hunters positively is... Well... The way they're already written. They don't need to be immune to the sleeping curse to be heroic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T13:06:40-07:00","id":218463,"title":"","content":"Here's a question: would they always write it off as something completely mundane or would they, if they were experienced in it, remember it as the abilities of another type of supernatural they were familiar with? For example, Random Hunter #48 sees Random Hunter #47 get torn apart by a mage who shapeshifted into a lion, could Random Hunter #48 then remember seeng his buddy get torn apart by a werewolf or would he just assume the guy he was after kept pet lions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T15:48:16-07:00","id":218578,"title":"","content":"I don't think the Sleeping Curse gets in the way of killing mages over much.<br /> <br /> I'd say a Hunter who wants to be all &quot;light in the darkness&quot; against mages should be more concerned about using perfectly innocent people as torches; the typical fictional bane of the witch hunter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T00:08:06-07:00","id":219934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=218463#post218463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a question: would they always write it off as something completely mundane or would they, if they were experienced in it, remember it as the abilities of another type of supernatural they were familiar with? For example, Random Hunter #48 sees Random Hunter #47 get torn apart by a mage who shapeshifted into a lion, could Random Hunter #48 then remember seeng his buddy get torn apart by a werewolf or would he just assume the guy he was after kept pet lions?</div> </div> </div> </div> The way I see it, the curse causes witnesses to see more mundane expanations for what happened, but honestly, how many weird circumstances would you have to notice around someone to figure out they're weird?<br /> <br /> So I think hunters would recognize mages as something weird, but ironically they'd probably see them as lesser magicians. Witches can shapeshift into bears, raise zombies, and and throw fireballs, mages would seem, thanks to the fog of memory, as souped up stage magicians using tricks and luck to superhuman effect. <br /> <br /> In short, I think they'd feel like they're in the movie &quot;Now You See Me.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T14:45:13-07:00","id":222467,"title":"","content":"I basically go the other way around. I don't like the supers to be immune to the Lie, Lunacy, Masquerade or others. All these things have flaws that can be exploited, and lead to better story imho. I prefer see my werewolf packmate spontaneously consume in presence of a supposed witch than seing a Mage throwing a fireball at him, even if in reality it's what's happening. It keep the mystery, and prevent turning horror into fantasy. I really liked the way Changeling 's Mask are handled toward the supernatural, and followed that lead. Now the Lie make people forget nearly every weird experience. It's ok for generic mortal. I don't think it's ok for any player's characters, even the most bland mortal you can play. It would, I don't know, invalidate most gaming session.<br /> <br /> In short: whatever you are, you won't see Magic, you won't see a Gauru face, but you will still witness some really strange event.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3648-nepher","name":"Nepher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3648_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T16:49:54-07:00","id":222566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you also remove Lunacy when your hunters are up against werewolves? </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah. Remembering what happened clearly when you witnessed magic is called <i>being a Sleepwalker</i>. If you want your Hunter characters to have that, give them the Merit. </div> </div> </div>Dave Brookshaw: the guy who can make a normal person feel like an incompetent jerk in twenty words and 5 seconds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3645-watercooler","name":"Watercooler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T00:24:08-07:00","id":222916,"title":"","content":"That is not my intention: Hunter's shapeshifters and witches are NOT Forsaken Uratha or Awakening mages. They're a simplified version of them warped to make them better antagonists in a Hunter game.<br /> <br /> If you use Awakening rather than Witchfinders to build your bad guys for a Vigil game, your characters will get roflstomped. That's not a failure of Awakening as a system - it's doing what it's meant to. The Hunters native to mage <i>are Mages</i> (fun fact - Banishers are the nWoD's version of cWoD's imbued hunters) because one of Mage's themes is how weak and blind Sleepers are compared to the Awakened.<br /> <br /> Witchfinders, Spirit Slayers, Mortal Remains, and Night Stalkers are there to get away from this kind of problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T00:58:30-07:00","id":222934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=222916#post222916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is not my intention: Hunter's shapeshifters and witches are NOT Forsaken Uratha or Awakening mages. They're a simplified version of them warped to make them better antagonists in a Hunter game.<br /> <br /> If you use Awakening rather than Witchfinders to build your bad guys for a Vigil game, your characters will get roflstomped. That's not a failure of Awakening as a system - it's doing what it's meant to. The Hunters native to mage <i>are Mages</i> (fun fact - Banishers are the nWoD's version of cWoD's imbued hunters) because one of Mage's themes is how weak and blind Sleepers are compared to the Awakened.<br /> <br /> Witchfinders, Spirit Slayers, Mortal Remains, and Night Stalkers are there to get away from this kind of problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aha, see, not having played very much Hunter or any Mage, this was not something I was aware of when cooking up this little thought experiment. I was not really even thinking about the mechanical implications of Hunter vs. Mage at all, I was just interested in The Lie as a story element and how Hunters might fit into a story that uses it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T06:49:49-07:00","id":223219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=222916#post222916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is not my intention: Hunter's shapeshifters and witches are NOT Forsaken Uratha or Awakening mages. They're a simplified version of them warped to make them better antagonists in a Hunter game.<br /> <br /> If you use Awakening rather than Witchfinders to build your bad guys for a Vigil game, your characters will get roflstomped. That's not a failure of Awakening as a system - it's doing what it's meant to. The Hunters native to mage <i>are Mages</i> (fun fact - Banishers are the nWoD's version of cWoD's imbued hunters) because one of Mage's themes is how weak and blind Sleepers are compared to the Awakened.<br /> <br /> Witchfinders, Spirit Slayers, Mortal Remains, and Night Stalkers are there to get away from this kind of problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems to be a fundamental tension between the game designers and many in the fanbase: in general, the game designers tend to prefer that each game be viewed as a separate universe in and of itself, as that gives the designers the maximum freedom to design each game precisely how they want it. Conversely, many fans would prefer that the gamelines be designed in the context of a shared universe so that they can have maximum freedom to mix and match elements from different gamelines as they see fit. <br /> <br /> Stuff like \u201cif you want to run mages and hunters together, pick either <b>Mage</b> or <b>Hunter</b> and disregard the other game\u201d is an example of a developer not wanting to compromise any of his vision for the sake of making games crossover-friendly, and is precisely the stance that players who want the games to <i>be</i> crossover-friendly find the most annoying. \u201cPick one gameline and interpret everything else through its lens\u201d was a key element of what gave the original World of Darkness its reputation for being hostile to crossovers; one of the big innovations of the new World of Darkness was that crossovers were much easier to manage, in part because you <i>didn\u2019t</i> have to say \u201cthis is using game X as the baseline\u201d. You could easily put Kindred and Uratha side by side and have them interact with each other without having to decide \u201cis this a <b>Vampire</b> game with Lupines in it, or is it a <b>Werewolf</b> game with Leeches in it?\u201d<br /> <br /> In the post-GMC era, the pendulum seems to be swinging back toward the original World of Darkness\u2019 way of (not) handling crossovers, with this business of the Lie and the Vigil being (thus far) the most blatant example: in the quote above, Dave is flatly saying \u201cyou should never do <b>Mage</b>/<b>Hunter</b> crossovers\u201d. If we accept this rationale, <b>Mage</b> and <b>Hunter</b> effectively exist in separate universes, because mages and hunters will never meet: mages will contend with Banishers instead, and hunters will contend with \u201cgutter magicians\u201d instead. This is precisely the sort of thing that ended up leading to the Fractured Cosmos section of <b>Ascension</b> (the <b>Time of Judgment</b> book for <b>Mage: the Ascension</b>) \u2014 and it\u2019s precisely what I <i>don\u2019t</i> want to see happen to the new World of Darkness. <br /> <br /> The \u201clights in the darkness\u201d premise of <b>Hunter</b>, as I understand it, is \u201cdon\u2019t underestimate ordinary people; they\u2019re capable of more than anyone gives them credit for.\u201d That\u2019s why <b>Hunter</b> has a \u201cMoral Support\u201d Tactic that can help a cell of hunters cope with Lunacy; and it\u2019s why I hope that the hypothetical Chronicle Book for <b>Hunter</b> will suggest ways for hunters to take the edge off of the Lie. I\u2019ve already suggested a comparable Tactic: an \u201cAfter Action Report\u201d where the cell of hunters compares notes and attempts to reconstruct what actually happened, giving them a way to get around the memory-wiping effects of the Lie. More generally, other gamelines have a tendency to describe how mortals are victims who are ultimately powerless against the monsters in the darkness; <b>Mage</b>\u2019s stance that Sleepers are weak and blind is just one such example of this. Conversely, <b>Hunter</b> says \u201cmortals aren\u2019t that helpless, after all\u201d. In a true crossover between <b>Hunter</b> and any other gameline, the hunters\u2019 arsenal of tricks ought to be as effective against the \u201cgenuine article\u201d as they are against the \u201ccheap knockoffs\u201d presented in <b>Hunter</b>\u2019s supplements.<br /> <br /> Put another way: games such as <b>Mage</b> are free to make sweeping statements about how helpless ordinary people are; but in the context of a shared universe, these should not be taken as absolute statements: there should always be cracks in the walls that cordon off mortals from everyone else; and <b>Hunter</b> should be all about chipping away at those cracks. This isn\u2019t a case of \u201cchoose one gameline to be dominant\u201d; this is a case of \u201cno one gameline gives you the whole picture\u201d \u2014 not even <b>Mage</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-09-2014, 10:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T07:09:12-07:00","id":223235,"title":"","content":"It's not like pitting mage against Kindred, or having mages and werewolves meet. That <b>Hunter</b> presented its cut-down mage rules without remembering Disbelief is a problem with <b>Hunter</b>, not <b>Mage</b>, and I'm not wasting space on it.<br /> <br /> Hunter's always been the outlier, crossover-wise; it has to be, to avoid requiring six+ corebooks. It's <i>better</i> this way, as a hunter Storyteller is more free to improvise monsters and solutions; there's no reason for your vampire antagonists in Hunter to be Kindred, either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T07:21:15-07:00","id":223245,"title":"","content":"But there\u2019s no reason for the vampire <i>not</i> to be a Kindred, either: hunters <i>should</i> be able to deal with Kindred, Uratha, Awakened, etc. <br /> <br /> Don\u2019t get me wrong, though: I\u2019m not asking you to \u201cwaste space\u201d on the fact that <b>Hunter</b> overlooked Disbelief; as you say, that\u2019s <b>Hunter</b>\u2019s problem, which is why I suggested that a future <b>Hunter</b> book should deal with it. But that\u2019s a different thing from arguing that hunters should never do crossovers, and should only deal with the rough approximations of the other gamelines that are presented in the various <b>Hunter</b> books. <br /> <br /> In fact, to my way of looking at things, the \u201crough approximations\u201d that <b>Hunter</b> features are examples of the new World of Darkness having \u201cmore things under the sun than are dreamed of in your philosophy, Horatio\u201d, to quote the Bard \u2014 where \u201cHoratio\u201d is a Kindred, or an Uratha, or an Awakened: the witches in <b>Witch Finders</b> <i>can</i> be used to approximate <b>Mage</b>\u2019s Awakened and <b>Second Sight</b>\u2019s thaumaturges; but they can <i>also</i> be used to approximate magicians who are neither of the above. The vampires of <b>Night Stalkers</b> don\u2019t just approximate the Kindred; they approximate the various vampires in <b>Wicked Dead</b>, and many other kinds of vampires that aren\u2019t addressed anywhere else in the new World of Darkness. Want to <i>really</i> mess with one of the Awakened? Confront him with one of these \u201capproximations\u201d: someone who wields magic but who isn\u2019t any type of magic user that the mage is aware of. <b>Hunter</b>\u2019s monsters have uses outside of <b>Hunter</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-09-2014, 10:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T07:41:21-07:00","id":223253,"title":"","content":"It's nice to have the approximations so that you can play Hunter without needing the books for what ever monsters you want to use as antagonists. But if I'm going to buy Mage (or whatever game line) anyway, it would be nice to be able to use Awakened (or whatever major template) in the game if I want to. We all understand that things will always be lopsided in crossover, and we all have our own house rules for dealing with those issues. It would just be nice if the books were written from an assumption that someone is going to try to use these elements together at some point, rather than an assumption that they should not ever touch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T10:41:56-07:00","id":223357,"title":"","content":"I don't really see why that assumption should be the default one, given each of the games is designed with themes and rules and sub-rules that can become extremely confusing for an ST to keep track of in a game. Losing those things means losing the themey goodness in favor of games which aren't optimized and aren't really written towards, with the very occasional exception.<br /> <br /> If people want to find their own awkward way to weld everything together, that's their prerogative, but asking the devs to do that work instead is just a recipe for unfun, thematically weaker content which would earn the ire of one group of players or another. Better to leave that one to the homebrewers to sort out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T11:43:22-07:00","id":223442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=223357#post223357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really see why that assumption should be the default one, given each of the games is designed with themes and rules and sub-rules that can become extremely confusing for an ST to keep track of in a game. Losing those things means losing the themey goodness in favor of games which aren't optimized and aren't really written towards, with the very occasional exception.<br /> <br /> If people want to find their own awkward way to weld everything together, that's their prerogative, but asking the devs to do that work instead is just a recipe for unfun, thematically weaker content which would earn the ire of one group of players or another. Better to leave that one to the homebrewers to sort out.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a difference between assuming that at some point someone will try to mash the subsystems together and assuming crossover as the default mode of play. I would not want the latter, as I feel it would make each game less compelling on its own. That's why I said, we understand that crossover will be wonky and we are comfortable houseruling to resolve those issues. I would just prefer if the attitude towards crossover was more &quot;sure, if that's what floats your boat&quot; as opposed to &quot;If you want Hunters in Awakening, use Banishers. If you want Mages in Vigil, use Witchfinders.&quot;<br /> <br /> To reiterate, I am fully aware Awakened mages will rotflstomp Hunters in a fight, and I am fully comfortable with that. I don't need (or want) cross-line balance. &quot;Balance is an illusion&quot; anyway. I would like it if the attitude towards crossover was a bit more welcoming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T11:59:34-07:00","id":223456,"title":"","content":"Hey - I <i>said</i>. Just give your Hunter PCs the one-dot Sleepwalker Merit.<br /> <br /> Mage has Banishers instead of Hunters the way Demon has Deva and Mummy has LDI.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T12:21:55-07:00","id":223491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=223245#post223245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But there\u2019s no reason for the vampire <i>not</i> to be a Kindred, either: hunters <i>should</i> be able to deal with Kindred, Uratha, Awakened, etc.<br /> <br /> Don\u2019t get me wrong, though: I\u2019m not asking you to \u201cwaste space\u201d on the fact that <b>Hunter</b> overlooked Disbelief; as you say, that\u2019s <b>Hunter</b>\u2019s problem, which is why I suggested that a future <b>Hunter</b> book should deal with it. But that\u2019s a different thing from arguing that hunters should never do crossovers, and should only deal with the rough approximations of the other gamelines that are presented in the various <b>Hunter</b> books.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's a strong argument to be made that there is no way to accomplish a happy medium between making Hunters feel like empowered normal people and the needs of power progression and maintaining the themes of the other lines. Tier 3 Hunters let you get close, although they do so at times by violating the themes of other lines (You really shouldn't be able to stop an Uratha from shapeshifting with seizure inducing grenades, for example, and the tone of a politically focused Requiem game is significantly injured by guys with weird guns making the Vampires violently expel Vitae from their pores or shooting bees out of their hands; lots of Hunter has no place in the other games), but some of those are straight up Supernatural templates; they don't feel all that much like empowered normal people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In fact, to my way of looking at things, the \u201crough approximations\u201d that <b>Hunter</b> features are examples of the new World of Darkness having \u201cmore things under the sun than are dreamed of in your philosophy, Horatio\u201d, to quote the Bard \u2014 where \u201cHoratio\u201d is a Kindred, or an Uratha, or an Awakened: the witches in <b>Witch Finders</b> <i>can</i> be used to approximate <b>Mage</b>\u2019s Awakened and <b>Second Sight</b>\u2019s thaumaturges; but they can <i>also</i> be used to approximate magicians who are neither of the above. The vampires of <b>Night Stalkers</b> don\u2019t just approximate the Kindred; they approximate the various vampires in <b>Wicked Dead</b>, and many other kinds of vampires that aren\u2019t addressed anywhere else in the new World of Darkness. Want to <i>really</i> mess with one of the Awakened? Confront him with one of these \u201capproximations\u201d: someone who wields magic but who isn\u2019t any type of magic user that the mage is aware of. <b>Hunter</b>\u2019s monsters have uses outside of <b>Hunter</b>. </div> </div> </div>This on the other hand is a really good use of Hunter, and the problems of brining the other lines into Hunter aren't really that present when it comes to brining (appropriate parts of) Hunter into the other lines. There's only really an issue going in the one direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T12:31:24-07:00","id":223502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=222916#post222916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is not my intention: Hunter's shapeshifters and witches are NOT Forsaken Uratha or Awakening mages. They're a simplified version of them warped to make them better antagonists in a Hunter game.</div> </div> </div> </div> However there is this little quote in the introduction to Spirit Slayers:<br /> <br /> &quot;Second, you can use this book and Forsaken hand-in-hand. Both books can easily be mixed together, with you as Storyteller pulling bits from each to keep players (be they controlling hunter or werewolf characters) on their toes.&quot;<br /> <br /> In fact Witchfinders says the same thing, with somewhat less clarity:<br /> <br /> &quot;If you don\u2019t have Mage: The Awakening , don\u2019t sweat it; you don\u2019t need it. Alternately, if you do have it, then this book becomes a different resource for you and your troupe. Some of the material contained within may serve to append your already-existent understanding, and in addition, this book can serve either as an antagonist book for Hunter wherein the mages play the antagonists, or it may serve as an antagonist book for Awakening where the hunters and their organizations play foil to your Awakened characters&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=223245#post223245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the witches in <b>Witch Finders</b> <i>can</i> be used to approximate <b>Mage</b>\u2019s Awakened and <b>Second Sight</b>\u2019s thaumaturges; but they can <i>also</i> be used to approximate magicians who are neither of the above.</div> </div> </div> </div> The paragraph above the one I quoted explictly says so; though I think that it could have done a better job if it described several styles of magic with advice for customising them for specific charachters. E.G. Here's some basic rules for magicians who barter for power, here's advice on customising them to fit their patron(s) (Though that might have needed more wordcount).<br /> <br /> <br /> Personally I think the best suggestion I've seen in this thread is Dataweaver's idea of an After Action Report Tactic. Though I point out that the True Sight of St. Abel mentions Quiescence by name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-09-2014, 03:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T12:35:46-07:00","id":223503,"title":"","content":"...Aaaaand here he is, right on cue.<br /> <br /> I'm out of the thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T13:25:19-07:00","id":223556,"title":"","content":"I don't understand the problem. There are plenty of options to mix Hunters with awakened mages if you want to. Give hunters have the sleepwalker merit, you could even give it to them for free when they first take up the vigil if you want to. You want empowered humans, then run a game that emphasises that. Saying that the awakened have to take an extra turn to cast a spell would probably balance things out a lot in favour of the hunters getting the drop on them. If you want to mix them, then figure out a way that pleases the players in your game, not some over-arching idea of thematic cohesion.<br /> <br /> Its kind of funny that these debates are usually brought up by fans of Hunter since Hunter has among the most flexible games mechanics going and its pretty easy to crib things in and out of it as you choose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1161,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","user":"Gravitas Man","date":". 08-09-2014, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","name":"Gravitas Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T14:32:52-07:00","id":223608,"title":"","content":"I've always felt that Hunter meshed really terribly with the other lines, more so than anything else. Simply put, some of their mechanics seems to hinge on other splats working in a way that they explicitly don't. As such I've always just taken Hunter to exist as its own separate little system because I feel it meshes so terribly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T15:06:17-07:00","id":223650,"title":"","content":"First off, I\u2019ve been wondering since the start of this thread why it isn\u2019t in the <b>Hunter</b> forum rather than the <b>Mage</b> forum, as the majority of the issues being broight up here are the sorts of things that <b>Hunter</b> ought to deal with, not <b>Mage</b>. <br /> <br /> The Sleepwalker Merit has been proposed a couple of times as a cure-all for this issue. And yes, if the Storyteller feels comfortable giving it to every player character in a <b>Hunter</b> game, that would indeed bypass the problem. <br /> <br /> However, I\u2019m assuming that Sleepwalker is a Supernatural Merit; and with reason: its effects involve granting a (minor) supernatural benefit (namely, exempting the person from a supernatural penalty that other have to contend with); and while the rules don\u2019t outright say so, the general nature of Supernatural Merits implies that they\u2019re not something that just anyone can pick up just by spending Experience on them \u2014 which holds true of Sleepwalker. If it isn\u2019t Supernatural, I\u2019d like to know the reasoning behind why not. As such, the above solution doesn\u2019t work for Storytellers who are wanting to emphasize the \u201cordinary people are capable of more than anyone gives them credit for,\u201d as Sleepwalkers aren\u2019t ordinary people anymore. It\u2019s true that <b>Hunter</b> isn\u2019t <i>exclusively</i> focused on this theme; Endowments, in particular, are a massive violation of it. But <b>Hunter</b> sequesters Endowments to Tier Three play for a reason: the themes in play at Tier Three are different from those in play at the lower Tiers. So there\u2019s a need for hunters to have a means of at least taking the edge off of the Sleeping Curse <i>without</i> flat-out negating it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T15:20:34-07:00","id":223654,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if Sleepwalker should be cosider a supernatural merit, it is suposed to have been the default state of humanity after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T15:22:34-07:00","id":223655,"title":"","content":"To answer the question of why I put it in the Mage forum, my theory that was the impetus of this thread kind of relies on two assumptions:<br /> <br /> 1. The Lie exists<br /> 2. Hunters are it's unwitting pawns<br /> <br /> 1 is a default assumption of Mage and is not a default assumption of Hunter, and 2 doesn't work well in a game where the Hunters are the protagonists. So the two key components of my theory don't play nicely with Hunter, but could be used to make them interesting Mage antagonists, as an example of how Sleepers can actually pose a threat to Mages if they are dependent enough on The Lie to fight for it. Therefore I felt it was more appropriate to put it in the forum for the template that would be the protagonists of such a story.<br /> <br /> That's also why I've been resistant to things like &quot;just use Banishers&quot; or &quot;just give them the Sleepwalker Merit.&quot; Sure, that's a thing I could do, but it would tell a very different story than the one I was initially proposing. The whole &quot;don't underestimate sleepers&quot; moral kind of falls flat if the Hunters are Sleepwalkers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-09-2014, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T16:02:48-07:00","id":223680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=223650#post223650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off, I\u2019ve been wondering since the start of this thread why it isn\u2019t in the <b>Hunter</b> forum rather than the <b>Mage</b> forum, as the majority of the issues being broight up here are the sorts of things that <b>Hunter</b> ought to deal with, not <b>Mage</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a very true thing you just said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=223650#post223650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sleepwalker Merit has been proposed a couple of times as a cure-all for this issue. And yes, if the Storyteller feels comfortable giving it to every player character in a <b>Hunter</b> game, that would indeed bypass the problem.<br /> <br /> However, I\u2019m assuming that Sleepwalker is a Supernatural Merit; and with reason: its effects involve granting a (minor) supernatural benefit (namely, exempting the person from a supernatural penalty that other have to contend with); and while the rules don\u2019t outright say so, the general nature of Supernatural Merits implies that they\u2019re not something that just anyone can pick up just by spending Experience on them \u2014 which holds true of Sleepwalker.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point being, if you're playing Hunter and you want the PCs to beat Quiescence, the easiest way is to make the Sleepwalker merit available to them. Or give it to them. Just say determined people can learn to fight through the Curse, whatever.<br /> <br /> Normally, the Sleepwalker isn't available to anyone who dealt with the supernatural a bit and wants to pay the XP. But normally, hunters can't beat the Quiescence by being more capable than anyone gives them credit for.<br /> <br /> Of course, as has been mentioned, the &quot;determined people can fight through it&quot; explanation isn't recommended if you're playing <i>Mage</i> and you want to include antagonist hunters. Because subjecting someone to the sight of Supernal magic should be fruitless and damaging to their mental health, because mages are isolated from Sleepers. In which case, the easiest way would be to say they're naturally Sleepwalkers and decided to band together and hunt mages. Second easiest is to say they all have supernatural merits or endowments. Third is to have someone with True Sight of St. Abel in the cell. Fourth easiest is to have at least one member who's in the Lucifuge or has some other supernatural Merit, who can then tell the others what really happened. Fifth is to have them all be Sleepers, and just say they aren't dumbasses, and they can very well be dangerous even if their memories get messed with.<br /> <br /> Personally, I like the After Action Report idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T16:03:57-07:00","id":223682,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=223650#post223650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So there\u2019s a need for hunters to have a means of at least taking the edge off of the Sleeping Curse <i>without</i> flat-out negating it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Simply using The Code to protect yourself from Integrity loss takes off the biggest edge. The Code and Willpower 5 should in theory be enough to play a Witchfinder; if you see magic and don't attack there and then you'll be left with a sense of unease which can lead to an investigation and witnessing magic again. Or if you have a film and The Code, you can remind yourself again and again without hitting a Breaking Point each time.<br /> <br /> Everything else is just a cherry on the top.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=223654#post223654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure if Sleepwalker should be cosider a supernatural merit, it is suposed to have been the default state of humanity after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really agree with the rigid distinction between natural and supernatural merits; but the question of how easy it is to trainyourself into sleepwalking is a relevent one.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T16:56:45-07:00","id":223718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=223682#post223682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Simply using The Code to protect yourself from Integrity loss takes off the biggest edge. The Code and Willpower 5 should in theory be enough to play a Witchfinder; if you see magic and don't attack there and then you'll be left with a sense of unease which can lead to an investigation and witnessing magic again. Or if you have a film and The Code, you can remind yourself again and again without hitting a Breaking Point each time.<br /> <br /> Everything else is just a cherry on the top.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is not how Quiescence works going by the FWC spoilers. Witnessing the magic again or reviewing film won't help. You'll continue to forget the second it stops. Sleepers cannot remember Supernal magic. Period. Willpower rating does not matter. There isn't a way to bypass that without Sleepwalker status.<br /> <br /> But you can certainly build to the point where a Hunter cell recognizes the signs that they, or someone else, is being impacted by Quiescence, and they can certainly try to figure out who the Witch is from that, by looking at who tends to be around those places when those effects have been occurring. They're just as likely to not get the right person, especially if the Mage in question is on to them, but that brings a nice thematic element of over zealous witch hunts; the Hunters can never really be sure they got the right person, and if they're fanatical enough, they can easily slip into casting an overwide net, and even then are just as likely to be targeting entirely innocent people on the basis of coincidences that line up with a flawed understanding of the effects of Quiescence.<br /> <br /> Edit: Supernal Magic can be thought of a bit like the Silence from Doctor Who, without the loopholes that're used to defeat them on the show. But even without those workarounds, there's still a way for a properly attentive person to start to notice that something is going wrong, even if they'll never be able to say what that is precisely, and if they can associate a person with that sense that something has been happening, and killing them makes it stop? Well... <br /> <br /> So there's a pattern of too perfect coincidences, or of sudden mass memory loss, or everyone has a significantly different recounting of events of some tragedy, or everyone has exactly the same recounting, it'll twig, and then they start researching for common elements. And this one guy has been involved in half a dozen such events. So they burn his house down while he's asleep. Etc, etc.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":614,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","user":"Eolirin","date":". 08-09-2014, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T18:31:27-07:00","id":223744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=223650#post223650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sleepwalker Merit has been proposed a couple of times as a cure-all for this issue. And yes, if the Storyteller feels comfortable giving it to every player character in a <b>Hunter</b> game, that would indeed bypass the problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Truth be told, I've been toying with the idea of giving Hunters a scalable merit called Conviction that goes from 1-5. Not the power stat from Mirrors but a lesser brother of it.<br /> <br /> What it does is basically applies a bonus when it comes to accurately remembering stuff that is affected by supernatural effects. The Lie is one of them but Lunacy is another and so on and so forth.<br /> <br /> The character that I have in my mind is Adam Jensen from Dues Ex: Human Revolution. Wrapped up to the gills in conspiracies but that doesn't matter. What does matter is they know where his loved one is and he simply will not stop looking until he's found her.<br /> <br /> But as people have mentioned, this isn't really a topic for the Mage forum.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T18:37:10-07:00","id":223748,"title":"","content":"Agreed that the memory loss aspect is the biggest problem. My \u201cAfter Action Report\u201d idea wasn\u2019t based on actually restoring the cell\u2019s memories; it was more of a \u201cBlind Men and the Elephant\u201d thing, except that instead of each blind man holding dogmatically to his own view of the Elephant, they actually put their heads together and reconstruct what it looks like. Nobody <i>remembers</i> the actual Supernal Magic that they witnessed; but by looking at the discrepencies in what they <i>do</i> remember, they\u2019re able to determine enough about what actually happened to have a shot at preparing reasonable countermeasures for the next time. <br /> <br /> That, and Moral Support (which is geared more toward resisting in-the-moment wigging out than after-the-fact amnesia), is the sort of thing I\u2019m thinking of in terms of there being cracks in the wall between mortals and the supernatural.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T18:55:31-07:00","id":223755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=223748#post223748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed that the memory loss aspect is the biggest problem. My \u201cAfter Action Report\u201d idea wasn\u2019t based on actually restoring the cell\u2019s memories; it was more of a \u201cBlind Men and the Elephant\u201d thing, except that instead of each blind man holding dogmatically to his own view of the Elephant, they actually put their heads together and reconstruct what it looks like. Nobody <i>remembers</i> the actual Supernal Magic that they witnessed; but by looking at the discrepencies in what they <i>do</i> remember, they\u2019re able to determine enough about what actually happened to have a shot at preparing reasonable countermeasures for the next time.<br /> <br /> That, and Moral Support (which is geared more toward resisting in-the-moment wigging out than after-the-fact amnesia), is the sort of thing I\u2019m thinking of in terms of there being cracks in the wall between mortals and the supernatural.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I hope a GMC overhaul of Hunter would ask the question of &quot;Why and What do you hunt?&quot; An answer like &quot;I hunt a Awakened because he killed my son when his spell went awry&quot; would get a benefit from trying to remember spells due to her target while if her Cell were targeting werewolves, she wouldn't get any benefit trying to remember because that's not her obsession (while another cell mate who is obsessed with werewolves would get a bonus).<br /> <br /> It gives focus on purpose of why Hunters hunt and exactly that focus that allows them to pierce the veil surrounding the supernaturals.<br /> <br /> The obvious drawback is the more obsessed you get, the harder it is to interact with normal society but that's already shown in the Code. :/<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T00:48:54-07:00","id":223934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eolirin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=223718#post223718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is not how Quiescence works going by the FWC spoilers. Witnessing the magic again or reviewing film won't help. You'll continue to forget the second it stops.</div> </div> </div> </div> Then play it on a continual loop while writing yourself notes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eolirin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=223718#post223718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Sleepers cannot remember Supernal magic. Period. Willpower rating does not matter. There isn't a way to bypass that without Sleepwalker status.</div> </div> </div> </div> I just read the spoiler again, and I can't see willpower being mentioned anywhere. Until we learn otherwise I'm going to assume that the old willpower rules are still intact; or than at exceptional success on the Breaking Point lets you remember something. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=223755#post223755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I hope a GMC overhaul of Hunter would ask the question of &quot;Why and What do you hunt?&quot; An answer like &quot;I hunt a Awakened because he killed my son when his spell went awry&quot; would get a benefit from trying to remember spells due to her target while if her Cell were targeting werewolves, she wouldn't get any benefit trying to remember because that's not her obsession (while another cell mate who is obsessed with werewolves would get a bonus).</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I think hunter handles that well already via your choice of Code. I could see a Merit about hatered, but I think making it a core aspect of Hunter might introduce problems when you get to non-violent groups like Net0 or the Null Mysteriis.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T01:59:16-07:00","id":223977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I just read the spoiler again, and I can't see willpower being mentioned anywhere. </div> </div> </div>I don't think it was in the official spoilers. I think DaveB just mentioned it in response to a question someone had in the long Fallen World Thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T03:14:18-07:00","id":224003,"title":"","content":"Yeah, trust us on this one, now people always forget Supernal magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T03:35:18-07:00","id":224028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=223934#post223934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Then play it on a continual loop while writing yourself notes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Notes that keep reading &quot;God this looks so fake, I can even see the wires&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T04:13:15-07:00","id":224032,"title":"","content":"Is there any spoiler saying you disbelieve while the magic is in plain sight?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T06:23:29-07:00","id":224060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=224032#post224032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any spoiler saying you disbelieve while the magic is in plain sight?</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't matter what you believe while you see it; all that matters is how you recall it at a later time.<br /> <br /> Neo probably thought that writhing probe robot looked pretty damn real while it was being inserted into him, and then he woke up from the dream.<br /> <br /> A video recording is even more removed, so you're not looking at the magic, you're looking at a thing in terms of your reconstituted memories of the magic.<br /> <br /> If a person writes down a note while a mage is right in front of them emitting fire from their hands saying that they totally saw a person doing that, when they look back at the note they'll arrive at any other conclusion than it being an accurate record of what happened and that their memory has been compromised.<br /> <br /> I'd say the World of Darkness has a fair number of people who've had too much exposure to magic and made too many attempts to find clever loopholes in the Sleeping Curse who are mistaken <u>by themselves</u> for having some kind of delusional mental illness by virtue of the fact that their memories don't seem to be lining up with apparent evidence of their past actions. Those aren't even the people where exposure to magic has actually caused degenerative mental strains to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T06:42:42-07:00","id":224066,"title":"","content":"No. The memory loss is explicitly an after-the-fact effect. <br /> <br /> I <i>do</i> think that declaring that Quiescence messes with recording devices and the like goes a little overboard. Quiescence should mess with <i>humans</i>, not <i>machines</i>. Yes, this gives hunters a way around the memory loss; but only if they take specific countermeasures intended to ensure they always have an accurate recording of what they\u2019re doing at all times \u2014 a recording that the police could confiscate, or that an enemy of the hunter could tamper with, or that could be destroyed in any number of different ways. And think of it: if a Network Zero member gets in the habit of trusting what his camcorder shows over even what <i>his own memory tells him</i>, that\u2019s a potential <i>weakness</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T07:06:33-07:00","id":224072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=224060#post224060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't matter what you believe while you see it; all that matters is how you recall it at a later time.</div> </div> </div> </div> I disagree. There are actually three important points:<br /> <br /> What you believe when you see it.<br /> What you believe afterwords.<br /> What you beleive even later after an investigation.<br /> <br /> <br /> If a hunter knows about the Sleeping Curse - say they heard about it from sleepwalkers on the Hunter grapevine (there is whole Conspiracies full of them after all) - and they rationalise a hunter being killed by a fireball as a gas main explosion. They'll still investigate, because it's still a dead hunter. If they realise that their memory doesn't fit reality and all the nearby gas mains are fine, and that everybody remembers it differently; that's probably enough for them to assume a witch.<br /> <br /> And if they also find notes from themselves; and they know/believe this phenomina exists; that's just further evidence - and probably more useful evidence since it might include the Mage's description.<br /> <br /> <br /> The only way the Sleeping Curse could be 100% effecitve is if it doesn't just modify memories of magic; but also changes your memories every time you find evidence that your memories don't match up to reality. I don't think it does that; partly because the blog post says &quot;in the presence of Supernal magic&quot; but mostly because a charachter realising that their memories don't match up to reality has much more story potential than never realising.<br /> <br /> If the Sleeping Curse has a 100% effective way of modifying memories of magic; but no protection from investigation afterwords beyond an imperfect pressure not to look closely at the supernatual - that hunter's have defeated by definition - I think that's where you get the maximum potential for stories.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T09:22:21-07:00","id":224203,"title":"","content":"I take issue with the premise that a person could follow that chain and still remain fully functional.<br /> <br /> They might become fairly effective at killing mages (and probably a few innocent people who unfortunately seemed to be mages), just at the expense of almost all other coherent social engagements.<br /> <br /> Nobody ever said that being a light shining in the darkness meant you get to still be happy or fulfilled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T09:27:09-07:00","id":224206,"title":"","content":"Did I ever say or suggest that they will be fully functional at regular life?<br /> <br /> Heck, the rules explicitly say they're not - drawbacks of the Code.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T19:17:12-07:00","id":224767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=224203#post224203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I take issue with the premise that a person could follow that chain and still remain fully functional.<br /> <br /> They might become fairly effective at killing mages (and probably a few innocent people who unfortunately seemed to be mages), just at the expense of almost all other coherent social engagements.<br /> <br /> Nobody ever said that being a light shining in the darkness meant you get to still be happy or fulfilled.</div> </div> </div> </div>True enough. More often than not, it means that you\u2019re a torch, burning yourself up to provide the light that drives away the darkness. <br /> <br /> Going a bit less poetically, my main concern is with a hard line being taken that says that Sleepers are metaphysically incapable of filling any role in the story other than \u201cvictim\u201d. I\u2019m concerned that the attitude is \u201cSleepers are intended to be victims; so any proposal of how they might be able to fight back on their own needs to be shot down.\u201d As opposed to, say, \u201cyes, there are ways for Sleepers to cope with the Lie and to be effective without resorting to undergoing some sort of supernatural transformation; but those ways exact their own toll from the Sleeper in question.\u201d The Code? Exempts you from Breaking Points at the cost of picking up some psychological problems of your own. Recording devices? Lets the determined Sleeper learn what actually happened; but can lead to reliance on said recording devices, which can fall into the wrong hands and/or be tampered with or destroyed. After Action Reports? Requires a lot of work to recreate the events that the Lie expunged \u2014 time that could otherwise be spent doing something more useful than damage control \u2014 and even then fails to recover everything that was lost. And so on. <br /> <br /> Becoming a Sleepwalker should be the only option open to a Sleeper for combatting the Lie that doesn\u2019t have a downside (unless you count the fact that Sleepwalkers no longer cause Dissonance or Paradox Risk); but that\u2019s different from saying that becoming a Sleepwalker should be the only option open to a Sleeper for combatting the Lie, period.<br /> <br /> Going back to the original post: another way to view the Vigil in <b>Mage</b> terms might be to say that Practical Experience is Arcane Experience for non-Awakened people. That is, a hunter who earns Practical Experience is getting vague hints of the Supernal Truths that the Lie seeks to conceal, enough to enable the hunter to chip away at the Lie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-10-2014, 11:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T23:46:03-07:00","id":224904,"title":"","content":"Ooh, I rather like that idea!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T07:08:51-07:00","id":225047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=224767#post224767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True enough. More often than not, it means that you\u2019re a torch, burning yourself up to provide the light that drives away the darkness. <br /> <br /> Going a bit less poetically, my main concern is with a hard line being taken that says that Sleepers are metaphysically incapable of filling any role in the story other than \u201cvictim\u201d. I\u2019m concerned that the attitude is \u201cSleepers are intended to be victims; so any proposal of how they might be able to fight back on their own needs to be shot down.\u201d As opposed to, say, \u201cyes, there are ways for Sleepers to cope with the Lie and to be effective without resorting to undergoing some sort of supernatural transformation; but those ways exact their own toll from the Sleeper in question.\u201d The Code? Exempts you from Breaking Points at the cost of picking up some psychological problems of your own. Recording devices? Lets the determined Sleeper learn what actually happened; but can lead to reliance on said recording devices, which can fall into the wrong hands and/or be tampered with or destroyed. After Action Reports? Requires a lot of work to recreate the events that the Lie expunged \u2014 time that could otherwise be spent doing something more useful than damage control \u2014 and even then fails to recover everything that was lost. And so on. <br /> <br /> Becoming a Sleepwalker should be the only option open to a Sleeper for combatting the Lie that doesn\u2019t have a downside (unless you count the fact that Sleepwalkers no longer cause Dissonance or Paradox Risk); but that\u2019s different from saying that becoming a Sleepwalker should be the only option open to a Sleeper for combatting the Lie, period.<br /> <br /> Going back to the original post: another way to view the Vigil in <b>Mage</b> terms might be to say that Practical Experience is Arcane Experience for non-Awakened people. That is, a hunter who earns Practical Experience is getting vague hints of the Supernal Truths that the Lie seeks to conceal, enough to enable the hunter to chip away at the Lie.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love the idea of practical experience being hints at the Supernal. It fits with the idea that pops up in the mage book stories and fluff that people get hints of the world beyond the Lie before they are distracted by it again, returning them again to sleep. Practical experience definitely seems to fit this.<br /> <br /> And I agree, sleepers aren't always the metaphysical victim. But they will always be the underdog. They lack the sheer cosmic power of a mage, or even abilities at the same level of other supernatural creatures, without giving up some of their own humanity to become like the things they fight. Attempts to fight back will always cost the hunter, as you pointed out, as even the Sleepwalker trait means you know longer make magic risky for the mage, or have the ability to dispel it by looking at it. Normal Mortals are often the guy who showed up to a knife fight unarmed (or possibly with a butter knife), and their opponents brought guns. This especially seems the case with the direction of post gmc supernaturals, such as the power boost for B&amp;S vampires. Couple the mechanics of the supernatural with the mechanics of the Lie, and they are at best tragic protagonist, doomed to fight against forces they can never truly equal or even understand without risking their sanity (essentially, mages become Cthullu)<br /> <br /> That said, there is a reason I love that the WoD is based on the <i> storyteller </i> system and that I am a <i>storyteller</i>: every story needs an underdog to root for, and fate seems to favor an underdog protagonist (the Acanthus in me won't let it be any other way.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 08-11-2014, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T10:04:04-07:00","id":225133,"title":"","content":"If the tone of the revised rules Mage is that Sleeper witch-hunters can't be a threat because they'll be completely mind-wiped by Disbelief, then I think it pretty much buries my interest in the game. And no, it's not a crossover issue or a problem when playing Hunter. I'm just not at all interested in a World of Darkness game in which mortal opposition to the PCs is doomed to failure. That supers couldn't just ignore mortals is what made me interested in nWoD, as opposed to oWoD. Comparing the Banishers to the oWoD Imbued doesn't help, because I really didn't like how oWoD Hunter presented mortals as completely powerless until the Heralds shoved powers into their heads.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I'm far from saying Mage is a bad game or that what the team is doing with it now is bad. To the contrary, it seems that there are some splendid ideas in the works. They're just disconnected from the stories I want to tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","user":"Morty","date":". 08-11-2014, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T12:51:18-07:00","id":225235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=225133#post225133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the tone the revised rules Mage is that Sleeper witch-hunters can't be a threat because they'll be completely mind-wiped by Disbelief, then I think it pretty much buries my interest in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>The rules are as they are because giving them the Sleepwalker merit for whatever reason you chose is the easiest thing possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=225133#post225133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just not at all interested in a World of Darkness game in which mortal opposition to the PCs is doomed to failure.</div> </div> </div> </div>That idea that a sleepwalker is somehow not a &quot;true&quot; mortalweirds me out a bit. I see no indication that the average sleepwalker is anything but a true, 100% purebred Xander style mortal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T14:28:16-07:00","id":225312,"title":"","content":"The problem with the Xander comparison is that the Buffyverse doesn\u2019t have the Lie: there are no Sleepers in that setting, so Xander is just like everyone else. <br /> <br /> Regardless of which (Sleepers or Sleepwalkers) is the <i>natural</i> state of humanity (and I <i>do</i> like the notion that Sleepwalkers hold that title), Sleepers are the <i>default</i> state of humanity. This makes Sleepwalkers the supernaturally empowered exception from the Sleeper perspective, and thus from the default <b>Hunter</b> perspective. The Xander-equivalent in the nWoD would be exceptional by virtue of not being subject to the Lie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T17:03:11-07:00","id":225418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=225312#post225312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sleepers are the <i>default</i> state of humanity. This makes Sleepwalkers the supernaturally empowered exception from the Sleeper perspective</div> </div> </div> </div>No, where are you getting that bit about supernaturally empowered?<br /> You automatically count as a sleepwalker if you are supernatural, but by itself being a sleepwalker does not make you any more supernatural than being able to hear colours or having non-average attributes.<br /> Sleepwalker status can be achieved by entirely mundane means, which includes any means that the ST decides fit becoming a sleepwalker.<br /> You could be born that way, become one through being exposed to supernal magic, to having a partial awakening, to just being that exceptionally wilful or awesome, from emotional investment or from thousands of other, 100% mortal sources.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=225312#post225312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> there are no Sleepers in that setting, so Xander is just like everyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, once he loses his eye he becomes decidedly unaverage and different from the &quot;default&quot; state of humanity in a way that is exactly as magical as being a sleepwalker is. The exact number of sleepwalkers in the world is up to the ST, but in most settings there will be proably more sleepwalkers than one-eyed humans.<br /> Which by your definition, assuming it's based on percentage of human population with that attributem makes Xander even more unnatural and further away from the default state of humanity in the setting than a sleepwalker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","user":"Joker","date":". 08-11-2014, 08:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T02:15:01-07:00","id":225786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=225133#post225133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the tone of the revised rules Mage is that Sleeper witch-hunters can't be a threat because they'll be completely mind-wiped by Disbelief</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder what the <b>chapter</b> on Sleepers will be like...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T02:48:49-07:00","id":225793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=225786#post225786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wonder what the <b>chapter</b> on Sleepers will be like...</div> </div> </div> </div>It starts with a quote from Memento. And anyone whose only idea of how Sleepers can interact with mages is &quot;hunters!&quot; has a stunted imagination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T03:54:13-07:00","id":225806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=225786#post225786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wonder what the <b>chapter</b> on Sleepers will be like...</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Mostly harmless&quot;<br /> Followed by 5 empty pages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T04:54:47-07:00","id":225836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=225793#post225793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It starts with a quote from Memento. And anyone whose only idea of how Sleepers can interact with mages is &amp;quot;hunters!&amp;quot; has a stunted imagination.</div> </div> </div> </div>OTOH, focusing on hunter/mage interactions in a thread entitled \u201cthe Lie and the Vigil\u201d doesn\u2019t strike me as a matter of stunted imagination; rather, it\u2019s a case of staying true to the topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T05:41:14-07:00","id":225859,"title":"","content":"The Sleepwalker merit as is, is probably the most empowering, Fuck Yeah Humanity element of the setting.<br /> It mortals taking one of the most powerful curses in the setting, cast by one of the most terrifying and powerful groups of the NWoD, and giving it the middlefinger. It's mortals using their willpower, or their inquisitiveness, curiosity or sheer bloody mindedness to break through one of the biggest supernatural effect ever created.<br /> It's looking up at the gods sitting in their thrones and telling them 'No. You don't control me'.<br /> <br /> Making it the default state of Hunters, an incidental side effect of picking up a shotgun to go after that vampire you saw? Cheapens it a lot,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=225133#post225133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the tone of the revised rules Mage is that Sleeper witch-hunters can't be a threat because they'll be completely mind-wiped by Disbelief, then I think it pretty much buries my interest in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a point of order, a group of Sleeper Hunters that is after a mage because they think the mage is a Slasher or other mundane monster is more dangerous to the mage than a group of Sleepwalker Hunter that is after them for being a wizard.<br /> Between Dissonance and increased Paradox a mage <i>really</i> doesn't want Sleeper Hunters after them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T06:40:25-07:00","id":225897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watercooler</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Much like your forum social skills.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">Personal attacks are a violation of rule 1.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T20:41:53-07:00","id":226755,"title":"","content":"I'm guessing sweeping insults that target no one in particular, yet everyone who thinks a certain way, is a violation of rule 1.b?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3645-watercooler","name":"Watercooler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T20:50:12-07:00","id":226760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watercooler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=226755#post226755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm guessing sweeping insults that target no one in particular, yet everyone who thinks a certain way, is a violation of rule 1.b?</div> </div> </div> </div>Attacking a group tends to be worse than an individual, yes.<br /> <br /> So is poking someone who actually has power over you in the places you dwell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T23:22:55-07:00","id":226815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watercooler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=226755#post226755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm guessing sweeping insults that target no one in particular, yet everyone who thinks a certain way, is a violation of rule 1.b?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is neither on topic, nor appropriate for public discussion. If you wish to discuss concerns regarding the rules and their enforcement, you should use the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\">contact us</a> link. If you believe a post to be in violation of the rules, you should use the report function. If you have something to discuss with a particular member that does not pertain to the topic, you should use the private messaging system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T03:24:34-07:00","id":226886,"title":"","content":"Hear him. If it weren't for the general atmosphere I'd be an active poster on these forums*.<br /> \u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014<br /> There's a line here with the Writers, Veterans and Moderators on one side and everyone else on the other. People with well known sigs are characters in the drama, everyone knows where they stand before they've said a word.<br /> \u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014<br /> If you're not a regular then you're conversational clutter, what's the point of posting? There's bound to be a regular who'll say a similar thing in a bolder manner and people will actually notice it.<br /> \u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014<br /> *it would also help if somebody would actually fix the forum so it doesn't strip line breaks out of posts from mobile devices, it was mentioned during the first week of the new forums by multiple people and it's still not been fixed."