ouble-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*facepalm*<br /> <br /> Dude. Yes, Dave was kinda insulting there. That wasn't very cool. Backtalking mods and throwing a fit about conspiracies is not the way to appropriately deal with that sort of situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're the only one to mention the ludicrous notion of a forum conspiracy. Don't try discrediting me or anyone else by attaching it to what we said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1370-ormag\u00f6den","name":"Ormag\u00f6den","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T04:16:24-07:00","id":226903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ormag\u00f6den</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=226890#post226890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're the only one to mention the ludicrous notion of a forum conspiracy. Don't try discrediting me or anyone else by attaching it to what we said.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, I'll be clearer. &quot;Throwing a fit and explicitly accusing moderators of willfully ignoring complaints directed toward certain favored persons&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T04:48:35-07:00","id":226913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=226903#post226903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sorry, I'll be clearer. &amp;quot;Throwing a fit and explicitly accusing moderators of willfully ignoring complaints directed toward certain favored persons&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll not only stop doing that, I'll edit it right out of the post and replace it with an unreserved apology, if you can quote me as saying that in the first place.<br /> <br /> Good luck with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1370-ormag\u00f6den","name":"Ormag\u00f6den","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T05:07:33-07:00","id":226934,"title":"","content":"Can we please stop this argument about arguing, and get back to the thread\u2019s actual topic? We\u2019ve got a dozen posts in a row so far that could be deleted <i>en mass</i> without harming the discussion that this thread is supposed to be about (yes, including this one).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-13-2014, 09:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T05:08:49-07:00","id":226935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ormag\u00f6den</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=226913#post226913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll not only stop doing that, I'll edit it right out of the post and replace it with an unreserved apology, if you can quote me as saying that in the first place.<br /> <br /> Good luck with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Watercooler. Watercooler did.<br /> <br /> I suppose after I realized you had posted while I was writing, I should have clarified who I was reacting to. Editing now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T08:34:15-07:00","id":227049,"title":"","content":"Sorry you're upset, Watercooler. I'll gladly edit that post out if you want.<br /> <br /> For the record, I try to answer as many people as I can. Even when I probably shouldn't. I am disinclined to take threads on this particular topic seriously after four years of being sniped at by certain individuals, and if you got caught up in that response, my bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":14,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","user":"Dave Brookshaw","date":". 08-13-2014, 11:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T09:04:31-07:00","id":227072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watercooler</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's actually no rule against criticizing someone with authority on these forums or anywhere else. And even if there was, that wouldn't stop me.</div> </div> </div> </div>What there are (or should be, I haven't actually checked) are rules against sidetracking an entire thread to make it about your grievances with the mod staff. Whatever else those grievances may be (well-founded? imaginary? juvenile? righteous?) the one term that can definitely describe them is &quot;way the fuck off topic&quot;. Take it somewhere else please?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T09:54:27-07:00","id":227084,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of a Phenomenal antagonist for Mages that isn't another Mage. It puts me in mind of the Agents from the Matrix (though one could make the argument that they're closer to Seers than Sleeping Hunters). Sleepers are a big threat to Mages, but the self-limiting factor is, of course, the fact that they <i>forget</i>. While we're not quite taking that away with Charlaquin's OP, we are changing the game up in a way that I like, though probably not for a long Chronicle.<br /> <br /> EDIT: For the record, I'm on the same page as Charlaquin regarding knowledge of Mage, maybe with a slight advantage because I've got a friend who I've been talking to who's been into NMage for a while. He mentioned that Abyssals kind of already fill that niche, and if somebody mentioned that upthread I apologize.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":1923,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","user":"BigDamnHero","date":". 08-13-2014, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T10:02:47-07:00","id":227107,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">I think Dataweaver and Joker are on to something.<br /> Sleepers have one advantage their awakened counterparts don't: Paradox. A wizard may try to bend us mere mortals to his will, but like a rubber band, we'll bounce back with a vengeance, likely poking that fool's eye out in the process. Further more, a sleeper doesn't have to be a hunter to hunt the supernatural. Take the police for instance, a magician may be questioned for being at the scene of the crime/freak incident. If he's caught lying, they'll hold him accountable for that crime. If he tells them the truth, they'll throw him into an insane asylum. If he tries to use sorcery to get out of this mess... well at that point, he's probably too far gone to help now. Note that this is a gross oversimplification of the point I'm trying to get across.<br /> I'd like to see this after action report tactic expanded upon.<br /> Has anyone thought of making willpower into a sort of pseudo power stat for hunters? It could be used to resist supernatural things like lie induced amnesia and whatnot. In order to activate it, the player must risk one of his character's willpower dots, and roll the rest.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/729-ocel","user":"ocel","date":". 08-13-2014, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/729-ocel","name":"ocel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T11:40:09-07:00","id":227166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ocel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=227107#post227107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">I think Dataweaver and Joker are on to something.<br /> Sleepers have one advantage their awakened counterparts don't: Paradox. A wizard may try to bend us mere mortals to his will, but like a rubber band, we'll bounce back with a vengeance, likely poking that fool's eye out in the process. Further more, a sleeper doesn't have to be a hunter to hunt the supernatural. Take the police for instance, a magician may be questioned for being at the scene of the crime/freak incident. If he's caught lying, they'll hold him accountable for that crime. If he tells them the truth, they'll throw him into an insane asylum. If he tries to use sorcery to get out of this mess... well at that point, he's probably too far gone to help now. Note that this is a gross oversimplification of the point I'm trying to get across.<br /> I'd like to see this after action report tactic expanded upon. Also, why not use willpower as a sort of pseudo power-stat for hunters whenever they resist supernatural compulsion. In order to activate it, you must risk one of your willpower dots and roll whatever's left. We could expand on that and say you can't use any that have been used already.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I actually had my players get arrested. They were lead by a mystagogue reclaimer and we're attempting to steal an artifact from a museum before it's display opened. The cops showed and the cabal very proudly went to counter them... And got their butts kicked. I pulled a story teller fiat and kept the Cabal alive (I had the scene play out like the opening of Leverage in the hospital), but between paradox, numbers and guns, the mages got taken down hard (to be fair, this was our 4th session, so they were pretty green both as players and stat wise, but still). They eventually got out of their mess due to their friendly neighborhood Mastigos and the wonder of the sleeping curse making people wonder why the cops opened fire on unarmed thieves, but the players realized that, as Harry Dresden has been kind to point out, that mortals as a whole are terrifying. <br /> <br /> I also love the idea of gambling willpower to remember for hunters. Good call.<br /> <br /> Also, one of the original posts said they didn't like the Vigil being a form of upholding the Lie since it undermines the idea of Hunters being a Light in the Darkness. But to me, that is a non-issue. Even if it is an aspect of the Lie, it does not undermine the benefit gained by destroying monsterous beings. It also could explain why the older/larger conspiracies get into so much questionable stuff (Grafting Abyssal parasites and other supernatural body parts to your agents? Hunting and Raping captured monsters? Tapping into demonic forces? Illegal supernatural drug cartels?): the nature of the Lie twists these conspiracies. I know it is mage once again forcing an explanation onto other lines (sorry) but I like the idea that the Lie has multiple ways to enforce itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T12:12:15-07:00","id":227218,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't really call it forcing an explanation anything, since if you don't like the explanation there's no need to use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T13:56:21-07:00","id":227320,"title":"","content":"Intruders raises the possibility that the Abyss might in some sense be the manifestation of the resentment of humanity towards to Awakened. It means that however bad the world is, it is ultimately the creation of humanity, not the God-kings of Atlantis.<br /> <br /> I think that's kinda the problem with the Light in Darkness theme as applied to Mage. It's a bit too complicated; but then that was kinda the theme of Witchfinder.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">A wizard may try to bend us mere mortals to his will, but like a rubber band, we'll bounce back with a vengeance, likely poking that fool's eye out in the process. </span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><br /> <br /> How? You're using a metaphor in place of explaining what would happen.</span> Indications are that the Seers for example do it all the time, and it doesn't obviously backfire on them, the sleepers get horribly messed up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">If he's caught lying, they'll hold him accountable for that crime. If he tells them the truth, they'll throw him into an insane asylum. If he tries to use sorcery to get out of this mess... well at that point, he's probably too far gone to help now.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><br /> <br /> Again, what happens? </span> The books already assume that most magi are quite capable of evading punishment if they want to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T14:37:25-07:00","id":227346,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:times new roman, times, serif\">The answer to both of your questions, Michael, is paradox. Yes, as you've pointed out, there are those exempt from this rule, cough, Seers. But that doesn't mean they can't be inconvenienced by Johnny Law, Van Hellsing or what have you. Also, those who abuse their gifts tend to lose them. What? You don't think a Seer can't lose the favor of his gods? </span><span style=\"font-family:times new roman, times, serif\">Humph. Well I do. They don't rule the fallen world, the Exarchs do... to an extent. And they won't hesitate to take their subordinates down a peg if need be. They aren't the only arch-masters/superpowers out there either. </span><span style=\"font-family:times new roman, times, serif\">T</span><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">he Guardians of the Veil tends to punish those who break the masquerade too, Seers or no.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/729-ocel","user":"ocel","date":". 08-13-2014, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/729-ocel","name":"ocel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T14:56:05-07:00","id":227364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman, times, serif\">But that doesn't mean they can't be inconvenienced by Johnny Law, Van Hellsing, or what have you.</span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm not disagreeing with that. It's just that annoyance isn't the same as an actual threat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman, times, serif\">T</span><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">he Guardians of the Veil tends to punish those who break the masquerade too, Seers or no.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><br /> <br /> That's indeed the much bigger worry; and it still undermines mortals.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman, times, serif\">Also, those who abuse their gifts tend to lose them. </span><span style=\"font-family:times new roman, times, serif\">What? You don't think a Seer can't lose the favor of his Exarch patron? Humph. Well, I do. They don't rule the fallen world, the Exarchs do... to an extent..</span> </div> </div> </div><br /> That sounds about right, but still if the Exarchs ever do it's not very common. And again, it's not the sleeper resisting, it's the Exarch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T17:00:52-07:00","id":233467,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Here's the thing... all those little inconveniences, they add up. A sleeper may not be able to catch a Seer for a supernatural crime, but he will try to catch 'im for a mundane one. The more often that Seer gets in trouble, the more likely he'll draw his patron's ire... or worse, its enemies. Again. The Exarchs aren't the only ones pulling the strings. They do not tolerate insubordination or failure. They punish it. Much like the God Machine. </span><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Mortals may not be able to deal the final blow, but they can certainly contribute to it.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/729-ocel","user":"ocel","date":". 08-18-2014, 11:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/729-ocel","name":"ocel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T23:15:45-07:00","id":233897,"title":"","content":"As to this - I once and more mentioned that God Machine can be very much Lie &quot;materialized&quot;, yes? God Machine wants the WoD as it is, sends Angels to &quot;correct reality&quot; and all. Now Hunters can work for Lie from different, unconsciousness point of view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T00:52:56-07:00","id":233951,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Here's the thing... all those little inconveniences, they add up. A sleeper may not be able to catch a Seer for a supernatural crime, but he will try to catch 'im for a mundane one. </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> I don't doubt they do, my point is that that isn't the same thing as an independent threat. The sleepers in this instance are basically terrain for the magi. The sleeper cop isn't the threat, it's the magi who are watching for suspicious activity, or the Exarch wanting to make a point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T20:00:31-07:00","id":236106,"title":"","content":"What I will probably rule is that being capable of Risking Willpower (i.e., being a Hunter on the Vigil or a Slasher on an Undertaking) blocks passive memory and curiosity blockers in a plot device kind of way. The same way GMC mortals are kind of assumed to be able to interact with the God-Machine's infrastructure even though they normally couldn't in a &quot;why else are we telling the story about them?&quot; sort of way, Hunters can remember spells and werewolves but are just as vulnerable to all other effects of the Quiescence or the Lunacy. The Quiescence might twist a Hunter into rejecting magic or distrusting it rather than forgetting about it entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T22:39:47-07:00","id":236202,"title":"","content":"Hmm? Outside of an Unseen Sense Merit, I don\u2019t recall any sort of assumption that mortals in GMC have any special ability to interact with Infrastructure that they normally wouldn\u2019t have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T22:42:15-07:00","id":236203,"title":"","content":"It's a general assumption they'll be able to interact with the story being told - not necessarily infrastructure in general, but the specific parts they're dealing with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T22:49:25-07:00","id":236209,"title":"","content":"Right; but there\u2019s no general assumption that mortals in general <i>can\u2019t</i> interact with the God-Machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T22:53:45-07:00","id":236210,"title":"","content":"Rather the opposite, in fact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T23:36:41-07:00","id":236224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=236209#post236209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right; but there\u2019s no general assumption that mortals in general <i>can\u2019t</i> interact with the God-Machine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course there is? The investigators in WoD core are individuals who have come into some kind of exceptional contact with the God-Machine; if the general run of humanity wasn't blinded by Concealment infrastructure, everyone would know about the Machine. An exception to the general norm that mortals can't see the Machine's gears. Even without Unseen Sense: God-Machine, a God Machine chronicle character is going to be exposed to It. <br /> <br /> In any event, the point was, I think amnesiac witch or werewolf hunters are dumb, but I am otherwise cool with Quiescence or Lunacy, hence the ruling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T00:21:44-07:00","id":236256,"title":"","content":"Concealment Infrastructure isn\u2019t the only, or even the main, reason why the God-Machine\u2019s existence isn\u2019t public knowledge. Another part of it is that Infrastructure sometimes takes forms that are easily mistaken for something else. I\u2019m not talking Concealment here; I\u2019m talking about a particular piece of Infrastructure being a stretch of the highway, or the rules and regulations of a bureaucracy. Often, humans are <i>part</i> of the Infrastructure, metaphorical cogs in the machine. The protagonists in the God-Machine Chronicle aren\u2019t special in that they\u2019re capable of something that ordinary humans aren\u2019t capable of; they\u2019re \u201cspecial\u201d only in that they know enough to look. <br /> <br /> All that said, I\u2019m not arguing about your main point, either for or against; I\u2019m only arguing against the line of reasoning that you presented to lead up to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T00:41:20-07:00","id":236268,"title":"","content":"Oh, I see what you mean. I was counting &quot;and in a way not represented by a formal merit, able to see certain infrastructure&quot; as &quot;special&quot;, but it also includes infrastructure that wasn't big-C Concealed in the first place, etc, that someone just happens to actually notice. That is there's nothing special about the character, but the God-Machine screwed up, or whatever.<br /> <br /> In any event, I'm basically talking about plot immunity. Some combination of events and traits leads a character to the workings of the Machine. Some combination of personal traits and experience leads to the Vigil, which (waves hands) happens to protect memories from passive tampering. There may be nothing special about the character, and sometimes the Lie or Lunacy just fizzle because it's the World of Darkness and nothing works correctly. Or there might be - the spiritual antibodies system of humanity building up strength through successive Vigils, doesn't really matter.<br /> <br /> I like breaking points for witnessing magic, so I keep that. I dislike amnesia, so I drop it. I like primal terror at seeing a werewolf, but dislike amnesia, so I drop it. I recognize for the setting to resemble the real world memory-erasing supernatural events need to be pretty ubiquitous, but there are exceptions, and I also think for the setting to resemble the real world, there needs to be a ton of mortal pushback - namely, Hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T18:42:36-07:00","id":244450,"title":"","content":"One thing to remember is that the Lie hides <i>magic</i>, not mages. A sleeper doesn't have to see the spells to start getting suspicious and a hunter sure as hell doesn't need to seem them to. Why do hunters <i>need</i> to accurately remember supernal magic to hunt supernal mages? Simply believing them to be unnatural as fuck is enough to set off most. That guy who seems to always bet on the right horse, in spite of not having a way to rig the race, he may be in league with a spirit or he may be Awake. That girl who everyone seems to adore but no one can remember more than 'that one with the hair and glasses right? Yeah she's awesome!,' could be a vampire or a mage. The lingering effects of magic, the broken minds, raped souls, and otherwise unnatural effects, are more than enough to get the wrong attention.<br /> <br /> If you need more than that to work with though, look at the witchunts of old and the writeup in Mage Core, people fear what they don't understand, they fear that kind of power. The Quiscience only hides the magic, the power and unholy insight you gain from it is what gets people wanting you dead. What's a more interesting game, one where the hunter is after you because he saw a fireball, or the one where he's after you because he's <i>afraid</i> of you, because he hates you for being so damn different? I'm assuming the mage's point of view here, being in the mage forum, but the point still stands; there are more complex reasons to provoke mage hunters than 'I saw them cast a spell.'<br /> <br /> That said, I could be totally wrong here and underestimating the lie.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1804-b-fox","name":"B.Fox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T19:48:56-07:00","id":244463,"title":"","content":"I'm in complete agreement with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T21:46:53-07:00","id":244531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>B.Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=244450#post244450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing to remember is that the Lie hides <i>magic</i>, not mages. A sleeper doesn't have to see the spells to start getting suspicious and a hunter sure as hell doesn't need to seem them to. Why do hunters <i>need</i> to accurately remember supernal magic to hunt supernal mages? Simply believing them to be unnatural as fuck is enough to set off most. That guy who seems to always bet on the right horse, in spite of not having a way to rig the race, he may be in league with a spirit or he may be Awake. That girl who everyone seems to adore but no one can remember more than 'that one with the hair and glasses right? Yeah she's awesome!,' could be a vampire or a mage. The lingering effects of magic, the broken minds, raped souls, and otherwise unnatural effects, are more than enough to get the wrong attention.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I largely agree, but the issue (for me is)<br /> <br /> -The Lie as it stands is a bit too perfect; the Hunter wouldn't remember something vaguely unnatural and scary happened, he wouldn't remember any supernatural element to the scene at all.<br /> <br /> -Amnesiac witch/werewolf/anything hunters just strikes me as extremely dumb. <br /> <br /> -I have an aesthetic preference for a wide array of failure modes for built-in supernatural defenses; weaknesses, cures, vulnerabilities, etc. &quot;Most of the time, Luna clouds the minds of men for us...sometimes, this fails...we don't know why or how..&quot; I also have a preference for hunters having a high degree of utility as dangerous antagonists.<br /> <br /> Hence, the Vigil grants that little extra subconscious push that unclouds the memories. Maybe not well, maybe not even immediately ,but there's always been a caveat with Lunacy or Dominate and what-have-you about the memories being repressed, how they might come out in dreams or hypnosis, that sort of thing. It's basically just the plot cover to have the patient at the insane asylum whose drawings represent what they did as a vampire slave that they otherwise can't remember, and so on. <br /> <br /> In actual practice, if a hunter is after a mage, he's probably not after him because he witnessed a spell. Who goes around casting random spells in front of those rare few people who take up the Vigil? It's more, if a hunter fights a mage, I want him to remember the battle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T23:39:00-07:00","id":244579,"title":"","content":"It is in no way shape or form perfect, for one thing I don't recall anything about it changing forensic evidence, just memories.<br /> <br /> A mage turns into a bear and mauls a guy, the wounds are going to say bear attack. The curse will mean that they won't remember the mage turning into a bear, but that doesn't mean it suddenly becomes more probable for a bear to maul someone in Manhattan, much less on the 21st floor of a hotel. <br /> <br /> If the memories say dog attack while the wounds say bear attack, than that's even more suspicious of something fishy going on. <br /> <br /> And hunters are vigilantes by nature, plenty of hunters would think &quot;a guy who trained bears to maul people&quot; is a problem solved by a couple of shotgun blasts to the face. <br /> <br /> Now of course a smart mage isn't going to rely on nature's jedi mind trick to cover their tracks, but a mage who actually is stupid enough to do so is a squeeky wheel begging for grease.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T23:42:51-07:00","id":244597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=236256#post236256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Concealment Infrastructure isn\u2019t the only, or even the main, reason why the God-Machine\u2019s existence isn\u2019t public knowledge. Another part of it is that Infrastructure sometimes takes forms that are easily mistaken for something else. I\u2019m not talking Concealment here; I\u2019m talking about a particular piece of Infrastructure being a stretch of the highway, or the rules and regulations of a bureaucracy. Often, humans are <i>part</i> of the Infrastructure, metaphorical cogs in the machine. The protagonists in the God-Machine Chronicle aren\u2019t special in that they\u2019re capable of something that ordinary humans aren\u2019t capable of; they\u2019re \u201cspecial\u201d only in that they know enough to look.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention the Concealment Infrastructure is half-assed at times and a few instances where Infrastructure is intended to be used by mortals.<br /> <br /> The God-Machine seems to only really care about being hidden due to the probable fact that if it was public, you would have humanity scrambling around like a bunch of ants who's nest has just been kicked over all the while screwing up the occult matrix via panicking and later, active resistance and while the God-Machine could crush humanity like a bug on a tank tread, it doesn't because that just complicates future plans.<br /> <br /> So it mostly keeps a low profile but a very apathetic one. It doesn't see the need to follow up on every human that stumbles upon it as much as a worker sees the need follow up on every wasp that visits his work bench when he works. It's only when they start getting in the way of his work that he feels the need to do something.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T09:12:37-07:00","id":244838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=244531#post244531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I largely agree, but the issue (for me is)<br /> <br /> -The Lie as it stands is a bit too perfect; the Hunter wouldn't remember something vaguely unnatural and scary happened, he wouldn't remember any supernatural element to the scene at all.<br /> <br /> -Amnesiac witch/werewolf/anything hunters just strikes me as extremely dumb.<br /> <br /> -I have an aesthetic preference for a wide array of failure modes for built-in supernatural defenses; weaknesses, cures, vulnerabilities, etc. &quot;Most of the time, Luna clouds the minds of men for us...sometimes, this fails...we don't know why or how..&quot; I also have a preference for hunters having a high degree of utility as dangerous antagonists.<br /> <br /> Hence, the Vigil grants that little extra subconscious push that unclouds the memories. Maybe not well, maybe not even immediately ,but there's always been a caveat with Lunacy or Dominate and what-have-you about the memories being repressed, how they might come out in dreams or hypnosis, that sort of thing. It's basically just the plot cover to have the patient at the insane asylum whose drawings represent what they did as a vampire slave that they otherwise can't remember, and so on.<br /> <br /> In actual practice, if a hunter is after a mage, he's probably not after him because he witnessed a spell. Who goes around casting random spells in front of those rare few people who take up the Vigil? It's more, if a hunter fights a mage, I want him to remember the battle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then again, most magic before four dots tends to be the sort of thing that's subtle or requires setting up in advance. I mean, there are exceptions (forces and life), but even then the spells that are blatant enough to need the lie are also obscenely vulgar. And once a spell becomes obscenely vulgar, then your going to have dissonance fucking with your magic anyway. Maybe the worse threat is that once the hunter knows, once the hunter has dug enough to know what the mage is capable of, the whole house of cards comes tumbling down.<br /> <br /> The Warlock's friends begin to forget about her, or hate her. The Acanthus and his horses just stops working for him. The magic begins to flee the taint of sleeping scrutiny as the hunter closes in on the source. The mages may escape once, maybe twice, but eventually their luck runs out. The Acanthus can no longer turn down the right corridors with the Vigil on his tail; and no Love spell or weave of hatred sticks to those hunters, they know too much, their awareness actively destroying the very spells that the Lie is trying to hide. Remember, if the mage has to cast on the fly they're screwed because even one hunter can eat the potency.<br /> <br /> Now if they get a decent spell out, great. Maybe they had a rote that rolled well or a ritual prepared. Even then the hunter can forget, his memory swallowed by the discordant shrieks of the abyss. He's still going to fight though. He's going to fight with tactics and endowments and weapons. When it's all said and done, a witches blood will be on his hands and he may not remember everything that went down. His mind stops in odd places and his memories tell of things that could not be. It would end like a horror movie almost, he'd try to get on with his life, try to put that horrible event behind him.<br /> <br /> If you've ever seen <i>The Skeleton Key</i>, that has a very similar vibe. Even at the final confrontation it's up in the air whether or not the supernatural is actually happening. (That said, it's also a good counterexample because the protagonist's investigation <span style=\"color:white\">allowed the magic work on her enough for the bad shit to actually go down.</span> (colored for spoilers)<br /> <br /> Still, I understand the complaint. Maybe there's a way to handle it, like how wolf blooded was handled in old <i>Forsaken</i>. Maybe something about the Vigil permits some sort of merit that adds to willpower for breaking supernatural occlusion effects. I mean, if I were to run a game with mortal or hunter PCs I'd give some sort of concession for the sake of fun, but that would be the best way of handling it without cheapening hunters or the Lie. (The question then becomes though, in setting is this merit inborn or something that someone develops?)<br /> <br /> Oh, at the risk of going totally off topic:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> If I were to run a game that was general crossover, what parts of the hunter setting (conspiracies, mechanics, etc.) would I need to look at and reconcile with the mage setting?</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1804,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1804-b-fox","user":"B.Fox","date":".  the code and me aren't getting along 08-30-2014, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1804-b-fox","name":"B.Fox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T12:28:32-07:00","id":244928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>B.Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=244838#post244838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Warlock's friends begin to forget about her, or hate her. The Acanthus and his horses just stops working for him. The magic begins to flee the taint of sleeping scrutiny as the hunter closes in on the source. The mages may escape once, maybe twice, but eventually their luck runs out. The Acanthus can no longer turn down the right corridors with the Vigil on his tail; and no Love spell or weave of hatred sticks to those hunters, they know too much, their awareness actively destroying the very spells that the Lie is trying to hide. Remember, if the mage has to cast on the fly they're screwed because even one hunter can eat the potency.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure it doesn't work that way.<br /> <br /> While the initial Warlock spell might have nudged people into the &quot;thinking this guy is friendly&quot; direction, after the initial spell all that remains are memories of what <i>happened</i>: namely they liked the Warlock; the spell is gone, there's nothing to dispel.<br /> <br /> As for the Acanthus: I have no idea what you mean by &quot;and his horses just stops working for him.&quot; But for the luck, as you pointed out, it's subtle, how do you (or rather, the Abyss) know what's really luck and what's actually Fate magic?<br /> <br /> There are other ways for the Hunter to close the trap, but simply disbelieving everything oughtn't work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T13:56:09-07:00","id":244985,"title":"","content":"There was the discretionary &quot;storyteller plot device&quot; +4 on Lunacy resistance even in the WtF corebook; I think declaring that people who have actively devoted some or all of their life to the Vigil aren't passively memory-wiped by supernatural effects. A professional werewolf hunter should probably be able to remember werewolves.<br /> <br /> I see the passive Lie as more akin to why most Sunnydale residents ignored the supernatural, but when you tell Oz why a guy just disintegrated he's able to believe you - you need a push or pull factor like the vigil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T14:37:31-07:00","id":245002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=244928#post244928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Acanthus: I have no idea what you mean by &quot;and his horses just stops working for him.&quot; But for the luck, as you pointed out, it's subtle, how do you (or rather, the Abyss) know what's really luck and what's actually Fate magic?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think something that would be really cool is that as the Hunter deepens his investigations or interactions with his target and starts piecing together the odd little things that his chances of Unravelling spells that would normally fly under his radar goes up. After all he's putting his target under additional scrutiny and he's on the lookout for any weird stuff at all because he's been having some memory problems since starting to go after this guy. For the Hunter it might look like his target is still getting lucky some of the time, but less than before the hunt started. For the Mage he's seeing even his subtler applications of magic whither away as the Hunter second guesses everything and suspects that anything the Mage is doing is actually fueled by his horrible, supernatural powers (And sometimes being right, and sometimes wrong).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T15:48:23-07:00","id":245043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=245002#post245002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think something that would be really cool is that as the Hunter deepens his investigations or interactions with his target and starts piecing together the odd little things that his chances of Unravelling spells that would normally fly under his radar goes up. After all he's putting his target under additional scrutiny and he's on the lookout for any weird stuff at all because he's been having some memory problems since starting to go after this guy. For the Hunter it might look like his target is still getting lucky some of the time, but less than before the hunt started. For the Mage he's seeing even his subtler applications of magic whither away as the Hunter second guesses everything and suspects that anything the Mage is doing is actually fueled by his horrible, supernatural powers (And sometimes being right, and sometimes wrong).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that's not how Quiescence works. The magic has to be something the Sleeper can directly witness in order to unravel it. If it's an instantaneous effect that occurs outside the Sleeper's direct sight or hearing then no Quiescence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T18:10:40-07:00","id":245114,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that cool idea is just that: a cool idea. That doesn't mean you can't use it; but acknowledging it as a house-rule is important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T21:55:38-07:00","id":245185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=245043#post245043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure that's not how Quiescence works. The magic has to be something the Sleeper can directly witness in order to unravel it. If it's an instantaneous effect that occurs outside the Sleeper's direct sight or hearing then no Quiescence.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not true either though, because if a Sleeper jumps to the conclusion, &quot;Only magic could do that!&quot; and it turns out only magic could do that, then they'll unravel the effect. A paranoid Hunter could jump to that conclusion all the time and manage to be right some of the time. If it has an effect that's completely beyond their senses and has no impact on them or things they witness then yeah they won't undo the spell, but when a Hunter is after a Mage then the things the Mage does to try and avoid or kill the Hunter are more likely to be noticed and dispelled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T00:03:06-07:00","id":245211,"title":"","content":"Arguably more likely (such a weird topic), but it still isn't going to affect anything outside of their perceptions. The Sleeper/Hunter would still need to SEE the effect of the magic (while the magic is active) to unravel it. It doesn't matter how unlikely or vulgar a spell that the Mage is casting when the Hunter isn't around.<br /> <br /> Thought, I'd be surprised if the Hunter activates Quiessence faster/more often than a regular Sleeper. It doesn't matter if he think's it's magic, it matters if he thinks it's IMPOSSIBLE to do without magic. &quot;I bet that Mage used magic to shoot me with his gun!&quot; doesn't do anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T00:17:12-07:00","id":245212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=245185#post245185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not true either though, because if a Sleeper jumps to the conclusion, &quot;Only magic could do that!&quot; and it turns out only magic could do that, then they'll unravel the effect. A paranoid Hunter could jump to that conclusion all the time and manage to be right some of the time. If it has an effect that's completely beyond their senses and has no impact on them or things they witness then yeah they won't undo the spell, but when a Hunter is after a Mage then the things the Mage does to try and avoid or kill the Hunter are more likely to be noticed and dispelled.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to have to ask for your source on that, because I have never seen anything that says a lucky guess unravels magic; I've only ever seen direct, Sleeper witnessing to unravel spells and only Vulgar or otherwise obviously magical effects to trigger Disbelief and cause additional Paradox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T07:55:00-07:00","id":245331,"title":"","content":"Just to clarify things: Disbelief just describes the forgetting of Supernal magic, and is specific to only magic that would be considered vulgar (including spells that are normally covert but have become improbable). The act of a spell falling apart under sleeper observation is not Disbelief, but instead <i>Unraveling</i>.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Unraveling</b><br /> A Sleeper who witnesses a vulgar spell might very well unravel that spell with the force of his Disbelief. The result is an extended action, accumulating successes over time. In the first turn in which the spell\u2019s effect is witnessed, roll the Sleeper\u2019s Resolve + Composure and compare the successes to the spell\u2019s Potency. If successes exceed Potency, the spell is dispelled. If they are equal to or less than the spell\u2019s Potency, the spell is unaffected.<br /> Every 10 minutes thereafter for the rest of the scene, roll again and add successes to the running total. Once successes exceed the spell\u2019s Potency, it is dispelled. A mage might try to hide the effect from a Sleeper, but if the Sleeper sees it again any time during the scene, his new Disbelief successes are added to his previous successes. (Note: If the action has moved on to another location, but the spell remains, Storytellers can assume one success on this roll per Sleeper per 10 minutes that pass, until the spell is unraveled. For example, a Potency 3 spell in a room with two Sleepers is unraveled in 20 minutes.) If a Sleeper leaves the scene of the spell, rolls are no longer made for him. </div> </div> </div>I always read that as the first turn the sleeper has a chance to roll for the Unravelling effect. In other words, throwing a single fireball won't trigger an unraveling simply because the effect finishes before the disbelief has a chance to unravel it. On the other hand, controlling a fire to turn it into serpents of fire to kill your opponents could trigger unraveling, though the potency would be high and likely not unravel quickly unless you do this I front of a group.<br /> <br /> Now, the rules for it specifies vulgar, but I would assume it extends to improbable covert effects. Still, covert spells that blend in wouldn't trigger unravelling at all. It also specifies that if the sleeper doesn't directly see the spell/it's effects, there is no unraveling. So studying a mage would only cause Unraveling of the spells that were directly observed long enough to break them down. <br /> <br /> Thus, in my reading of the rules, a Fate mage wouldn't only have to worry about unravelling if they relied too much on improbable effects and the same spell was observed by that hunter repeatedly providing those effects.<br /> <br /> Then again, this is all for 1e. With the removal of vulgar vs. covert in 2e, I am not sure ow this will play out (though it may be tied to the whole&quot;obvious magic thing&quot;). Or it could be something new, or not even exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 08-31-2014, 11:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T21:49:42-07:00","id":245853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=245212#post245212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to have to ask for your source on that, because I have never seen anything that says a lucky guess unravels magic; I've only ever seen direct, Sleeper witnessing to unravel spells and only Vulgar or otherwise obviously magical effects to trigger Disbelief and cause additional Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if a coincidence happens and the Hunter guesses magic and happens to be right, isn't he witnessing it?<br /> <br /> Mostly I'm just extrapolating some possibilities from what Dave has said on the matter. Could I be misinterpreting? Yeah, sure, but it's still a fun idea and I think would do Hunters a lot of good while not just giving them a hand-wave solution to end-running the Lie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 09-01-2014, 01:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T01:25:15-07:00","id":245945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, if a coincidence happens and the Hunter guesses magic and happens to be right, isn't he witnessing it? </div> </div> </div>He'd need to know supernal magic exists already, and the Quiescence is wiping that from their memory. Also, I think you'd need to be more than a vague guess; you'd need that to be an instinctive reaction.<br /> <br /> I think it seems kinda redundant anyway. Even without seeing any magic, they're still sinister conspiracies of people who hang around in weird clothes, discuss magic, and occasionally murder people. That the Hunter occasionally has gaps in their memories around them, and fighting them causes bizarre bouts of insanity is only the icing on the cake for why you should go after them.<br /> <br /> I'd use Banishers for the more warped Hunters with a tie to the Lie/Abyss. The 1e version pretty explicitly says that's what they're for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T02:30:57-07:00","id":246016,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s a reason why thtey\u2019re no longer calling it Disbelief: it has nothing to do with what the Sleeper believes, and everything to do with the shard of the Abyss that\u2019s lodged in the Sleeper\u2019s soul reacting violently to the Supernal Magic that has just been brought to its \u201cattention\u201d. <br /> <br /> If the Sleeper isn\u2019t present when the Supernal Magic is, there\u2019s no Unraveling (or Dissonance, as it\u2019s now called). OTOH, the Sleeper\u2019s memories are <i>well</i> within the Abyssal shard\u2019s ability to muck with long after the magic is gone. Thus, the ongoing memory-wiping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T02:52:44-07:00","id":247661,"title":"","content":"Which is fine, but I suspect it might be more interesting if the effects of that abyssal curse varied with individuals. In my formulation, it isn't as strong with some as it is with others - still causes Integrity loss for hunters but their memories stay intact - but you could spin it out further to a whole host of horrific variations. Some rare sleepers become addicted to the witnessing of magic, others have so strong an abyssal shard magic does not work at all in their presence, another immediately copies the spell into their soul and can cast it themselves but it always causes paradox, some sleepers die if they witness the Supernal, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T04:55:43-07:00","id":247741,"title":"","content":"Some of the suggestions you\u2019re making strike me as being more of a Banisher thing than a Sleeper thing; but really, the only part of your suggestion that I disagree with is the insistence that if you\u2019ve taken up the Vigil, your memories remain intact. If that works for you, fine; but I find it more interesting if the default assumption is that hunters are, by default, just like everyone else when it comes to the Vigil, and that any special resistance or vulnerability an individual hunter may have takes the form of a Tactic, a Merit, or a Persistent Condition. <br /> <br /> Bear in mind, though, that my own opinion on the Vigil is that there are essentially three playstyles that <b>Hunter: the Vigil</b> should support: <br /> <br /> \u2022 an \u201cordinary people\u201d playstyle, where the only difference between a hunter and a mortal is setting elements such as membership in a hunter org (specifically, no rules changes \u2014 not even Risking Willpower or Practical Experience \u2014 are assumed to be in play in an \u201cordinary people\u201d <b>Hunter</b> Chronicle unless the Storyteller explicitly allows them). <br /> \u2022 a \u201chunters are special\u201d level where all hunters get access to a few special benefits such as Practical Experience or Risking Willpower unless the Storyteller explicitly forbids them, and potentially have access to a number of additional Merits and special rules that don\u2019t cross the line into the supernatural. This playstyle is specifically geared to groups who prefer their protagonists to be a cut above the regular mortal, but don\u2019t want to venture into supernaturally empowered mortals. <br /> \u2022 \u201care they human, or monsters?\u201d, where the hunters are assumed to have access to some sort of Supernatural Merits, and the line between hunter and prey is a blurry one. <br /> <br /> This, rather than \u201ccell, compact, or conspiracy?\u201d is how I prefer to think about Hunter tiers; and \u201chunters get to keep their memories\u201d strikes me as being a \u201ctier two, but bordering on tier three\u201d thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T05:08:32-07:00","id":247747,"title":"","content":"I very like idea that Lie is changing Hunters perspective and almost actively hunting monsters, or at least directing them in &quot;proper way&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T06:15:13-07:00","id":247778,"title":"","content":"I suppose it depends on how supernatural you see resistance to the passive Lie effects. I don't see it as particularly unnatural, since the Lie is itself a supernatural condition and it's already supposed to have a subtle effect on humanity as a whole causing broad - but not universal - avoidance of curiosity into the strange. Since Hunters are, presumably, the kinds of people who have had the blinders ripped off in the first place, going one step further and saying they get to remember magic or werewolves strikes me as reasonable; those effects have to work within the sheltered psychological terrain of the general population and, well, hunters are outside of that. I don't see distinguishing between &quot;normal person&quot; and &quot;person who knows the supernatural exists and may even know specifically that magical spells and werewolves exist&quot; in terms of the effects the passive Lie/Lunacy effects have on them offers a superpower to the latter category. If you're a fifth generation Heritage House hunter trained and taught from birth that magic exists, or if you're the victim of a murderous spell and you've spent years undergoing memory regression therapy to regain your memories of that night...it doesn't strike me as damaging to the themes of Hunter if you'e able to remember magical spells or werewolves. <br /> <br /> Heck, if you want to make it really cruel, you could say that, since the memories don't fade, the Integrity loss is worse for Hunters than it is for regular Sleepers...<br /> <br /> But, really, this is just a metagame thing. It's a pain in the ass to turn every werewolf hunting or witch hunting storyline into a repressed memory memento investigation, and I just think amnesiac hunters are silly unless they're hunting a monster whose whole theme is memory eating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T07:02:27-07:00","id":247809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=247778#post247778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose it depends on how supernatural you see resistance to the passive Lie effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. It depends on how exceptional you see hunters being. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=247778#post247778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see it as particularly unnatural, since the Lie is itself a supernatural condition and it's already supposed to have a subtle effect on humanity as a whole causing broad - but not universal - avoidance of curiosity into the strange. Since Hunters are, presumably, the kinds of people who have had the blinders ripped off in the first place, going one step further and saying they get to remember magic or werewolves strikes me as reasonable;</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t buy into the notion that hunters have had their blinders ripped off. As well, it doesn\u2019t strike me as reasonable that the Sleeping Curse, which exists specifically to conceal Magic from mortal eyes, would fail at that purpose just because a mortal has seen something unnatural. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=247778#post247778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">those effects have to work within the sheltered psychological terrain of the general population and, well, hunters are outside of that. I don't see distinguishing between &quot;normal person&quot; and &quot;person who knows the supernatural exists and may even know specifically that magical spells and werewolves exist&quot; in terms of the effects the passive Lie/Lunacy effects have on them offers a superpower to the latter category.</div> </div> </div> </div>As you pointed out before, the Lie is a supernatural effect. I\u2019m not drawing a distinction between people who don\u2019t believe in the supernatural and those who do, because <i>belief in the supernatural is not relevant to the Lie</i>. You can be utterly convinced that magic is real and still succumb to Quiescence\u2019s memory-clouding effect, just as you can be a Sleepwalker who doesn\u2019t believe in magic. To the extent that they correlate at all, Belief follows from being a Sleepwalker, not the other way around. That is, a Sleepwalker will have an easier time believing in the supernatural because it isn\u2019t hidden from him; but even assuming that he <i>does</i> believe (which is not guaranteed), that\u2019s not the <i>cause</i> of him being a Sleepwalker. Likewise, the Sleeping Curse isn\u2019t <i>caused</i> by not believing in magic; instead, you\u2019re less likely to believe in magic if you have no recollections of ever having seen it. If anything, being a Sleeper encourages skepticism about magic, not the other way around. This isn\u2019t <b>Mage: the Ascension</b>. <br /> <br /> That\u2019s why <b>Mage 2e</b> is dropping the term \u201cDisbelief\u201d. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=247778#post247778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, really, this is just a metagame thing. It's a pain in the ass to turn every werewolf hunting or witch hunting storyline into a repressed memory memento investigation, and I just think amnesiac hunters are silly unless they're hunting a monster whose whole theme is memory eating.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you\u2019ve said. That\u2019s why I outlined those three different playstyles: it\u2019s not a matter of it being silly for hunters to have to deal with amnesia where witches and werewolves are concerned; it\u2019s a matter of <i>you not liking that approach</i>. Personal preference, not objective superiority. You prefer your hunters to be exceptional, which is fine; and if <i>you</i> want to run your games in such a way that all of your hunters remember magic and werewolves, go for it! But please, stop with the insistence that there\u2019s something wrong with running <b>Hunter</b> games where forgetting magic is a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-03-2014, 10:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T07:22:44-07:00","id":247832,"title":"","content":"I didn't mean to insist there was anything wrong with the other way of doing things! I think Hunter, as written, distinguished hunters from the mortals of the core book in an analogous way to how all the supernatural templates work. I like this approach because I like the idea that hunters are out of step with regular people in certain important ways due to their exposure to the supernatural. If you're using Hunter as an expansion to the blue book line, then that kind of &quot;A Hunter has entered the secret world and cannot go back&quot; attitude doesn't fit.<br /> <br /> I'm hoping the actual rules when we see them have a more elegant way of dealing with this, or maybe when Hunter rolls around we'll see a good workaround. Since &quot;Sleepwalker&quot; is a one-dot merit and presumably can be acquired through experience normally, it also just makes sense for a lot of hunters to be sleepwalkers if they deal with witch-hunting on a regular basis. Which would also imply that such hunters are more likely to awaken, which has interesting consequences for mage-focused conspiracies. Likewise, there could be a tactic that handles this adequately.<br /> <br /> \u200bIronically, I'm not as convinced all active supernatural powers should constitute immunity - just ones of supernal origin. Joe Blow Psychic whose power comes from the ancient occult genetic engineering of the God-Machine doesn't have any particular in-setting justification to not be under the Sleeping Curse, after all. Vampires and even Ghouls are immune, without really any reason given there's no supernal origin to vampirism - it's for crossover support purposes between the major templates and their key servants. And I see the logic to that and how it could extend to Hunters. <br /> <br /> But, well, it's a Curse, not a matter of belief, so conceivably only in-setting revocations of the Curse should apply. <br /> <br /> Perhaps the easiest compromise is to borrow Supernatural Tolerance from <i>Skinchangers</i>, turn it into a merit, and say it applies to the Sleeping Curse, Lunacy, etc. Anyone with adequate justification for being hardened to the supernatural might pick it up - psychics, ghouls, hunters, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":543,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","user":"Professor Phobos","date":". 09-03-2014, 10:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T07:43:47-07:00","id":247843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=247832#post247832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't mean to insist there was anything wrong with the other way of doing things! I think Hunter, as written, distinguished hunters from the mortals of the core book in an analogous way to how all the supernatural templates work. I like this approach because I like the idea that hunters are out of step with regular people in certain important ways due to their exposure to the supernatural. If you're using Hunter as an expansion to the blue book line, then that kind of &amp;quot;A Hunter has entered the secret world and cannot go back&amp;quot; attitude doesn't fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Conversely, I\u2019ve advocated removing anything from <b>Hunter 2e</b>\u2019s character creation that can be construed as \u201ca template\u201d, because I <i>don\u2019t</i> like the implied distinction between hunters and \u201cregular\u201d mortals. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=247832#post247832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm hoping the actual rules when we see them have a more elegant way of dealing with this, or maybe when Hunter rolls around we'll see a good workaround. Since &amp;quot;Sleepwalker&amp;quot; is a one-dot merit and presumably can be acquired through experience normally, it also just makes sense for a lot of hunters to be sleepwalkers if they deal with witch-hunting on a regular basis. Which would also imply that such hunters are more likely to awaken, which has interesting consequences for mage-focused conspiracies. Likewise, there could be a tactic that handles this adequately.</div> </div> </div> </div>AFAIK, being a Sleepwalker doesn\u2019t make you any more prone to Awakening than anyone else is. Also, Dave has said before that breaking the Sleeping Curse is supposed to be hard on the person who is becoming a Sleepwalker: spending an Experience to pick up a one-dot Merit doesn\u2019t reflect that at all. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=247832#post247832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bIronically, I'm not as convinced all active supernatural powers should constitute immunity - just ones of supernal origin. Joe Blow Psychic whose power comes from the ancient occult genetic engineering of the God-Machine doesn't have any particular in-setting justification to not be under the Sleeping Curse, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>On this point, I agree with you; and it <i>is</i> ironic, because the \u201call psychics are Sleepwalkers\u201d notion is motivated by the exact same reason why you prefer hunters to be able to keep their memory after witnessing Supernal magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T23:44:48-07:00","id":248663,"title":"","content":"The lie not affecting other major splats makes sense in that the Lie affects humans, and other major splats aren't. With the possible exception of Geist, but you've got another dude in your soul. <br /> <br /> It affecting ghouls and the like is more problematic, since you're still just a human at that point. But that could be saying more about the human condition of the ghoul than weirdness of the Lie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T12:59:56-08:00","id":1058528,"title":"","content":"What I'm gathering is that being around a Mage is probably going to be the most normal a Hunter is going to be as he's not going to suspect magic/monsters for a change as a result of the Lie. I would have preferred it worked like Lunacy myself and that Sleepwalkers be analogous to Wolf-Blooded but I didn't make the games. I'm curious as to why there was such emphasis on hiding magic and werewolves from mortals, to my knowledge Vampires don't have anything that naturally does this other than traditions and guidelines. Ah well, shouldn't be too hard to retool the Lie as a form of Lunacy and I already use the After Action Report Tactic. I'm wondering if DFRPG might be better to invest in though, I've already spent a bunch on CofD but if they're going the same route as oWoD then I might have a bunch of books to sell if anyone is interested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T16:28:20-08:00","id":1058640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Jub-Jub</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=1058528#post1058528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious as to why there was such emphasis on hiding magic and werewolves from mortals, to my knowledge Vampires don't have anything that naturally does this other than traditions and guidelines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf and Mage both deal with magic that operates on much more global forms of contagion, whereas Vampire occupies the awkward split between &quot;'feed responsibly' covers most of the problems a personlike vector for the Curse can cause without deliberately fucking about&quot; and &quot;most of the <i>non-</i>personlike vectors for the Curse are either ignorant of the concept of limiting exposure or actively derisive of it&quot; \u2014 there's no consistent secret world of vampirism that threatens to infect the mortal population besides the Kindred and a whole lot of weird bullshit that can't or won't keep the lid on on its own because it's a cursed letter opener or a tainted plot of land or a Strix, so the bulk of the hush-up operations are dealt with on the Kindred end of things through cultural taboos like the Traditions or dedicated conspiracies like the Invictus. Things still leak through the gaps between the boards, because that's the nature of vampirism and the supernatural at large, but needing to secure enough blood to reanimate your corpse until dawn for seven nights a week is generally harm enough and reason enough to try and keep a lid on your unfortunate diet and allergies as one of the Kindred.<br /> <br /> Werewolf has some of the same problems as Vampire does, with the added wrinkle of their lunar heritage actively degrading people's ability to resist spiritual influence with repeated exposure and a substantial chunk of the Shadow being sentient, mobile, and disinclined toward their entire species. Add to this the Doylist angle of &quot;werewolf society diverges quite strongly from mortal common knowledge about werewolves and the warping of memories via the primal terror of the void-watcher's children serves as a workable explanation for the lack of useful information.&quot; (It's difficult for me to guess at how much this feeds back into Vampire's thing, because I have not done stringent research on where the emergence of the vampire as a <i>gregarious</i> analogue for exploitative nobility as a concept sits relative to the publication of Masquerade, but on an in-universe level globalization and the development of the internet probably work as a reasonable explanation for the greater number of social vampires in modern vampire fiction in a setting where the Kindred exist.)<br /> <br /> As for Mage, there's a couple of things, some of them to do with the framework of the game and some of them to do with the way magic is within the setting \u2014 the fact that this is a game set in a world that can at least superficially pass for our own has to address the fact that this is also a game whose mages can create a lot of highly visible effects, and this is also a game where magic is generally treated as a sacred thing of a kind with the secret rites of a lot of the cults of antiquity and their modern imitators. Add in the fact that Awakened magic is almost exclusively man-made with minimal vectors for direct Supernal interference with reality, then look at the one <i>big</i> example of direct Supernal interference with reality and note that its conceptual basis comes from a religious format that takes the &quot;sacred things hidden from society at large&quot; in the other direction, add in the force that turns unity with the divine into a supernatural gambling addiction, and you have a pretty decent grounding for Why Magic Is Hidden.<br /> <br /> A lot of these notably stem from the common points of contagion and paranoia \u2014 &quot;supernatural forces are virulent and antithetical to humanity&quot; and &quot;most humanlike supernatural beings that are designed to be playable have some investment in humanity continuing to exist&quot; go a long way toward not wanting a parliament of shadow-owls to engage in wanton mass-murder in the town square.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T17:37:21-08:00","id":1058699,"title":"","content":"IT'S ALIIIIIIIIIVE!!!<br /> <br /> Gotta be honest, this is kind of an embarrassing thread to see resurrected. My understanding of Mage has evolved quite a bit since I started it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T17:52:32-08:00","id":1058706,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure that if Jub-Jub resurrects any more dead threads, he deserves the title of Honourary Moros.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T18:02:15-08:00","id":1058714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=1058706#post1058706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure that if Jub-Jub resurrects any more dead threads, he deserves the title of Honourary Moros.</div> </div> </div> </div>My Favorite Path!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T11:14:51-08:00","id":1059082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=1058699#post1058699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IT'S ALIIIIIIIIIVE!!!<br /> <br /> Gotta be honest, this is kind of an embarrassing thread to see resurrected. My understanding of Mage has evolved quite a bit since I started it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh. Yeah; and since then, the info we have to work with has evolved considerably. M2e is out, and includes a Merit for Sleepwalkers that says that you can become a Sleepwalker after repeated exposure to Awakened Magic<sup><span style=\"font-size:8px\">\u2605</span></sup>; H2e is in the works, and we now know that the Code will be a more central aspect in 20th than it was in 1e; and finally, Crossover Chronicle has been announced, which is likely to be the true home of actual Mage/Hunter crossover issues.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:gray\"><hr />\u2605 though I'm still if the opinion that a hunter shouldn't need to become a Sleepwalker to deal effectively with Magic. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T11:22:23-08:00","id":1059083,"title":"","content":"There is a twist on this idea; Hunters could be not just the instruments of Lie, they could be instruments of Abyss. Abyssal shards in them see magic and instinctively try and to dismantle it; they start guiding future Hunter to find and destroy more magic, first by witnessing it, next by killing mages. Abyssal Resonance Merit from Banishers books works wonderfully for those Abyss hunters, and even Eyes of the Abyss will make them a real threat to mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T11:32:10-08:00","id":1059089,"title":"","content":"Actually, I have toyed with the idea of hunters as serving the Lie once. That ended up with a project I named as the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/864775-heirs-of-the-lie-also-known-as-project-o-x-sum-up-post\">Heirs of the Lie</a>, which its basic principle is hunters who serve the Lie, each under the guidance of a different Iron Seal. They are bastards, sure- but the idea was to show the side of Exarch which protects humanity (even if out of selfish and tyrannical motivations), and that even the worst of mankind can still light a candle.<br /> <br /> So- is the Vigil a product of the Lie? don't know. Could the Lie serve the Vigil? Hell yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T06:19:14-08:00","id":1059466,"title":"","content":"I'm honestly of the opinion that, in a Mage game, mortal hunters are hideously outclassed and quickly are got rid of or manipulated into being pawns of one Mage or another.<br /> <br /> Yes, this doesn't seem very fair or nice, and it goes against the tradition of supporting the underdog, but Mage is about Mages and the world us neither nice nor fair in the face of hubristic shapers of reality.<br /> <br /> That said, Mages aren't the only witches out there, and I think Mage does benefit from the presence of mortals with the odd minor supernatural talent, in fact, they probably outnumber Mages. A few mortal hunters might successfully go after someone who can talk to ghosts and communicate telepathically. That said, they might regret it when that minor occultist gets rescued by their full actual Mage patron, who is comparatively a scary, scary bastard.<br /> <br /> I run all the game lines as being in separate worlds myself. Just prefer it that way. So I have no issue with Hunter and Mage clashing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T06:51:21-08:00","id":1059478,"title":"","content":"Well, it's now an issue for Crossover Chronicle to deal with. Given Dave's previous stance on the issue (which very much aligns with your position), I won't be surprised if XOC opens its Mage/Hunter section with something to the effect of \u201cthe hunters will get curbstomped\u201d; what I'm going to be most interested in is what comes after that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T06:53:09-08:00","id":1059479,"title":"","content":"A distinct part of Mage is that Mages are actually exceptionally powerful and privileged people who <i>think</i> they're the underdog, when they can be bothered to turn their thoughts towards a higher cause. A Mage getting hunted by people is just chickens coming home to roost as someone reminds them they're only the hero of their <i>own</i> story, not necessarily everyone else's.<br /> <br /> There's an entire Order whose central thesis is based around being able to dismiss a Sleeper who says &quot;What the hell is wrong with you!?&quot; by answering &quot;You don't know what you <i>really</i> want, and that's why I am in charge!&quot;.<br /> <br /> And yeah, there's <i>way</i> more Sleepwalkers, psychics, thaumaturges, and other &quot;low&quot; magic occultists making magic amulets, building spirit traps, or monkeying with destiny than there are Mages in a given region. Them ending up fearing their Mage patrons is a thing that tends to happen a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T07:17:11-08:00","id":1059485,"title":"","content":"I tend to feel that Mages often have a network of occultists, minor psychics, fringe academics, sleepwalkers, occasionally proximi and such who they cultivate over time.<br /> <br /> Whether they are relatively benevolent teachers, mentors and patrons or ruthless bastards who use them as pawns and sacrifices, or wherever in between, varies wildly. But I think it's often the case. In that situation, mortal hunters do have a role to play. I'd potentially use them as threats to that exact network.<br /> <br /> Like, you get a phone call from one of your sleepwalker occultist allies. She's worried, and thinks she's being followed. As it happens, she is, by a cell of hunters convinced she's a witch who is responsible for things that you actually did, but whatever. Do you abandon your own shit to go and check to see if she really is being followed? Every time? You can find out the truth quite easily, probably, but you have a number of people, and you can't always be running after them when they jump at shadows. In that sense, mortal hunters are a source of pressure on others that you value, people you can't always protect, especially as some of those hunters are actually pretty dangerous, determined and careful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T07:24:45-08:00","id":1059488,"title":"","content":"That does tie nicely into the Mage theme of &quot;Sure, you can do it. But should you do it?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T07:44:26-08:00","id":1059501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=1059485#post1059485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to feel that Mages often have a network of occultists, minor psychics, fringe academics, sleepwalkers, occasionally proximi and such who they cultivate over time.<br /> <br /> Whether they are relatively benevolent teachers, mentors and patrons or ruthless bastards who use them as pawns and sacrifices, or wherever in between, varies wildly. But I think it's often the case. In that situation, mortal hunters do have a role to play. I'd potentially use them as threats to that exact network.<br /> <br /> Like, you get a phone call from one of your sleepwalker occultist allies. She's worried, and thinks she's being followed. As it happens, she is, by a cell of hunters convinced she's a witch who is responsible for things that you actually did, but whatever. Do you abandon your own shit to go and check to see if she really is being followed? Every time? You can find out the truth quite easily, probably, but you have a number of people, and you can't always be running after them when they jump at shadows. In that sense, mortal hunters are a source of pressure on others that you value, people you can't always protect, especially as some of those hunters are actually pretty dangerous, determined and careful.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I <b><i>really</i></b> would not want to be the Hunter that killed an ally or friend of an Awakened mage, no less a sleepwalker favored by an entire Consilium or Order.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I imagine if a mage switched one of his Obsessions to &quot;enact hideous revenge resulting in a fate far worse than death,&quot; that Hunter and everyone he cares about may very quickly regret their life choices (and the mage would get beats all the while).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T07:44:54-08:00","id":1059503,"title":"","content":"One arrogance that people forget Mages fall prey to is the arrogance of forgetting that the world they inhabit is a lot scarier for the people they pull into the fringes of it. If you encourage that sleepwalker to develop her academic knowledge of ancient ritual practices, and provide her with texts and such to assist, and start to use her as a reference in your own studies and investigations, then you're putting her at risk. And sure, you mitigate that risks from some sources, like other Mages. But from ordinary mortals driven to the Vigil? Maybe not. Maybe you forget, of overlook, and you're busy, and you have a lot of people to patron just like her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T07:48:17-08:00","id":1059504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=1059485#post1059485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to feel that Mages often have a network of occultists, minor psychics, fringe academics, sleepwalkers, occasionally proximi and such who they cultivate over time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget that actual game Merits allow mages to control entire mystery cults, either openly or the power behind the scenes.<br /> <br /> For every Awakened mage in an area, there might be dozens or more of related and affiliated &quot;lesser&quot; supernaturals and/or occult followers, servants and allies. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T08:07:15-08:00","id":1059522,"title":"","content":"Turning this around, hunters are often portrayed as being in over their heads. A Chronicle where a hunter cell investigates a Mystery Cult with the intent of dismantling it could easily lead them into conflict with an Awakened mage with influence over said cult. And while the most likely outcome would be the cell getting trounced, the mage's own hubris might work to their favor leading her to consistently underestimate them. I mean, they're just Sleepers; how dangerous can they be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T08:11:34-08:00","id":1059525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=1059501#post1059501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I <b><i>really</i></b> would not want to be the Hunter that killed an ally or friend of an Awakened mage, no less a sleepwalker favored by an entire Consilium or Order.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I imagine if a mage switched one of his Obsessions to &amp;quot;enact hideous revenge resulting in a fate far worse than death,&amp;quot; that Hunter and everyone he cares about may very quickly regret their life choices (and the mage would get beats all the while).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but they don't know that. They don't know about your power, because why would they? Even if they know you exist, the Lie will force them to forget any display of terrible potency you have, so you can't easily scare them off.<br /> <br /> And let's say because you don't help that Sleepwalker, she is attacked and hospitalised. You swear terrible vengeance, find the guy who did it... and discover that he is a broken man, shattered by a madness he couldn't comprehend when it took his family into the darkness. He is convinced your friend is an agent of darkness and trying desperately to bring light into a dark world. You just going to kill him? Really? You might, but you might not be able to bring yourself to do it, and instead, you begin to investigate the mystery of what happened to make him like this.<br /> <br /> In such a story, the Vigil provides an antagonist, a source of pathos, and a mystery. Sounds good!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T08:30:46-08:00","id":1059532,"title":"","content":"That's one possibility. Another possibility is the Fitful Slumber Merit: though the hunters started out as Sleepers, repeated exposure to Supernal magic has turned them into Sleepwalkers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T08:38:59-08:00","id":1059539,"title":"","content":"Honestly? I don't think I'd ever bother trying to portray them as threats. My players are clever and they'd probably undercut any intent I had of making them threats by just taking them out, unless I engaged in a bit of bullshit plot armour, which they'd notice and not appreciate. Why try, when there's so many good threats, and you can use Hunters in a different way that they're more effective at?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T08:43:46-08:00","id":1059540,"title":"","content":"You're still looking at it from the perspective of Mage protagonists. But what if the <i>hunters</i> are the protagonists?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T08:46:03-08:00","id":1059542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=1059540#post1059540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're still looking at it from the perspective of Mage protagonists. But what if the <i>hunters</i> are the protagonists?</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I wouldn't send them against a Mage.<br /> <br /> I'd send them against the Witches from Hunter.<br /> <br /> Especially as I'd just constantly feel like I was pulling punches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T08:47:42-08:00","id":1059544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=1059540#post1059540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're still looking at it from the perspective of Mage protagonists. But what if the <i>hunters</i> are the protagonists?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why do you hate your players?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T08:54:03-08:00","id":1059550,"title":"","content":"Yeah that's basically my feeling. I create a Mage with, like, Mind 3, Space 2, I dunno, Fate 1. Lol those Hunters are all going to die, let's be honest. And it's not like Mages are public figures. If they can find out who they are, and if they can figure out what they're up to, and if they can figure out how to get to them... the Mage will neuter them with pretty casual ease. And that's a starting character Mage.<br /> <br /> Note; for me this is a feature not a bug. I like that Mages are hella powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T08:56:36-08:00","id":1059553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=1059540#post1059540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're still looking at it from the perspective of Mage protagonists. But what if the <i>hunters</i> are the protagonists?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If the Hunters were protagonists, I''d be playing a different game and reading a different forum. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That's precisely why the different themes and obvious power differential among the various splats and game lines often causes so much trouble in crossover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T09:06:57-08:00","id":1059556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=1059544#post1059544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do you hate your players?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't. Mage vs. Hunters is an uphill battle for the hunters; but that's why I mentioned that Hunter is quite often about being in over your head. As well, mage as \u201cmonster of the week\u201d (err, story) is a bad choice. Such a conflict more naturally revolves around a Chronicle, with the hunters starting out going up against the mage's Mystery Cult while the mage initially dismisses the hunters as \u201cjust Sleepers\u201d not worthy of her attention. By the time you reach the climax of the Chronicle, the mage will have reason to regret underestimating them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T09:08:27-08:00","id":1059558,"title":"","content":"I allways thought of hunters as mortals that evolved and became resistant to the lies of the supernatural, be it the Masquerade, Lunacy, Qiescense, etc... I consider them no sleepwalkers, nor servants of the Lie.<br /> <br /> My thought is that Hunters are humans that have become resistant or inmune to a sickness. For me, the key word is evolution, or if you want, their minds or souls are able to accept and digest the concept that &quot;there are monsters out there&quot; without stripping their sanity to pieces. It keeps the theme of hunter centered on the sense of humanity.<br /> <br /> Of course they have fear of a Werewolf (oh my, of a Werewolf and of a natural grizzly bear running to them while roaring fiercely and disposed to chomp the hunter's head), but that fear is caused no more by Lunacy (well, this is the way I treat hunters).<br /> <br /> This moment of clear awareness may come from a traumatic experience, a natural curiosity, a fanciful mind, a breaking point or born already with it. The fragment of the abyss is there, but it affects the mortal no more. Is useless. The Lie cannot manipulate the Hunter no more, no for blinding him nor for using him. Nor this fragment, nor another one. He is inmune.<br /> <br /> What prevents them from awakening? I like to theorize that the Vigil makes them more aware of their humanity. It reinforces their sense of being human, and that sense of belonging is what prevents them from awakening. This sense of belonging can take any form: racial superiority, racial survival, destroy any menace to human race, serve and protect, academic curiosity, scientific coldness, and all the grey tones in between you can think about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","user":"dourden","date":". 03-07-2017, 12:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","name":"dourden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T09:10:04-08:00","id":1059561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=1059553#post1059553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If the Hunters were protagonists, I''d be playing a different game and reading a different forum. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That's precisely why the different themes and obvious power differential among the various splats and game lines often causes so much trouble in crossover.</div> </div> </div> </div> Which is why I'm interested in seeing what they come up with in Crossover Chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T09:12:20-08:00","id":1059563,"title":"","content":"Also, before awakening, Mages were humans with a natural disposition, curiosity and willpower to seek misteries, to see beyond. A Banisher was also a human that wanted to know, and that knowledge scared the hell of him.<br /> <br /> Hunters never wanted to know, or if they wanted, it was never at the level of becoming a Mage.<br /> <br /> As I said in the post before, I like the theme of human evolution, resistance and sense of belonging for Hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","user":"dourden","date":". 03-07-2017, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","name":"dourden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T09:13:37-08:00","id":1059564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=1059556#post1059556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't. Mage vs. Hunters is an uphill battle for the hunters; but that's why I mentioned that Hunter is quite often about being in over your head. As well, mage as \u201cmonster of the week\u201d (err, story) is a bad choice. Such a conflict more naturally revolves around a Chronicle, with the hunters starting out going up against the mage's Mystery Cult while the mage initially dismisses the hunters as \u201cjust Sleepers\u201d not worthy of her attention. By the time you reach the climax of the Chronicle, the mage will have reason to regret underestimating them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have, in fact, used that very premise in a long-running Hunters in Rome game. The antagonist was one of the forebears of the Seers of the Throne, and he wanted to thrust Rome into chaos because a Fallen Rome was easier to keep Asleep than an Enlightened Empire. He had a number of mystery cults and political allies in several provinces as well as connections in the Parthian Empire, and the vast majority of the game was taking down his allies. The catch, of course, was that he was actually keeping them alive and helping them because he honestly thought their attempts to stop his plans were just creating even more chaos, a la 'I win either way.'<br /> <br /> A Mage makes a really great Big Bad or Man Behind The Man in a Hunter game. But that's like, <i>one </i>Mage, not a Cabal or, god forbid, an Order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T09:15:35-08:00","id":1059565,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12340_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12340\" data-vbnamecard=\"12340\">dourden</a>: note that, officially at least, the default hunter is not immune to the Lie. That said, hunters who survive confronting Supernal and/or Abyssal threats long enough can purchase the Fitful Slumber Merit, which nullifies the Abyssal shard in their soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-30-2023, 08:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T09:29:04-08:00","id":1059570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=1059565#post1059565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12340_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12340\" data-vbnamecard=\"12340\">dourden</a>: note that, officially at least, the default hunter is not immune to the Lie. That said, hunters who survive confronting Supernal and/or Abyssal threats long enough can purchase the Fitful Slumber Merit, which nullifies the Annual shard in their soul.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Didn't know this. Thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","name":"dourden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T11:20:45-08:00","id":1059621,"title":"","content":"I've been toying with the idea of letting mortal player characters (not even hunters) go up against a mage if I ever get around to ST:ing a campaign of my own that I've been thinking about for a while. But despite knowing that two of my potential players read this forum I'm going to describe how I'd do it:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">First of all, it would be an unaffiliated mage with neither a cabal or order to fall back on.<br /> Secondly, I'd carefully select Arcana dots that don't have an obvious use that straight up incapacitates one or several of the characters with a single spell. I'm not saying which Arcana because that'd be too much of a spoiler if I get around to using this idea.<br /> Lastly, I would not portray the most competent of mages. They would definitely not be stupid, but lack of training and experience can give the players an edge if it comes to a straight up fight. It's not like the mage can take five minutes to peruse the book to find the perfect spell to cast in actual combat. For example, a Matter mage would not necessarily realize they could end the fight instantly by solidifying the air around all enemies.<br /> <br /> And yes, I realize this mage would be severely limited compared to any player controlled mage ever, and that 99% of all mages will wipe the floor with a group of mortals, regardless if they're experienced hunters.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-07-2017, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T14:28:44-08:00","id":1059753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=1059561#post1059561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Which is why I'm interested in seeing what they come up with in Crossover Chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's entirely possible it will be the same answer we've been getting here, which is &quot;don't&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T14:34:03-08:00","id":1059756,"title":"","content":"You have a better chance when the hunters are sleepwalkers, so that might be a recommendation. There's a strange resistance regarding it from some but it takes care of the otherwise unavoidable barriers to hunters.<br /> <br /> Anyways it seems like it's going to be more fluff-oriented so we'll probably see glimpses of compacts or conspiracies that work alongside mages or against them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T14:50:11-08:00","id":1059763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=1059753#post1059753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's entirely possible it will be the same answer we've been getting here, which is &quot;don't&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;Or give them the Sleepwalker Merit&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T14:52:39-08:00","id":1059764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=1059763#post1059763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> &quot;Or give them the Sleepwalker Merit&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I still don't quite get why so many people seem so resentful of this option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T15:01:35-08:00","id":1059769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=1059753#post1059753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's entirely possible it will be the same answer we've been getting here, which is \u201cdon't\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div> Unlikely, as that would demonstrate an appalling lack of imagination.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=1059756#post1059756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have a better chance when the hunters are sleepwalkers, so that might be a recommendation. There's a strange resistance regarding it from some but it takes care of the otherwise unavoidable barriers to hunters.</div> </div> </div> </div> For my part, I've been resistant to a whole cell of hunters <i>starting out as</i> Sleepwalkers, without a reasonable in-story justification for it. But between Fitful Slumber and the ability to ascend the tiers and eventually pick up Endowments, there are reasonable ways for everyone in a cell to acquire Sleepwalker status \u2014 and that's <i>without</i> seeing what H2e or XOC will bring to the table.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=1059756#post1059756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyways it seems like it's going to be more fluff-oriented so we'll probably see glimpses of compacts or conspiracies that work alongside mages or against them.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm sure there will be fluff-oriented stuff in there. But my understanding is that one of the motivating factors behind XOC is to address mechanical concerns of crossovers: the sorts of things that would occasionally have found their way into nWoD books such as \u201cwhat happens when a werewolf enters the Hedge\u201d or \u201cwhat happens when a vampire experiences Disquiet\u201d. ChroD books have steered clear of such matters thus far, and it turns out that they've done so because the devs have been wanting to consolidate all such matters into a single book (or perhaps a line of books?), namely XOC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T15:02:24-08:00","id":1059770,"title":"","content":"I don't believe that providing Hunters with the Sleepwalker Merit demonstrably or meaningfully alters the extreme power disparity between the Awakened and what are otherwise normal humans, particularly for purposes of crossover. In fact, it removes one of the only small defenses that humans have against the Wise, automatic Paradox risk with obvious magic and dissonance.<br /> <br /> I envision a broken and burned Hunter slowly and painfully dying in the critical care ward of a hospital, only now he can vividly and accurately recall the who and how of the demise of his entire cell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T15:09:49-08:00","id":1059774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=1059769#post1059769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Unlikely, as that would demonstrate an appalling lack of imagination.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Or a simple and quite rationale acknowledgement that due to the different themes and priorities of each game line, power disparities do indeed exist, and since inter-splat crossover was not only not considered important in most of the games' design (with the apparent exception of Beast), but was arguably even counterproductive for individual lines, some crossover permutations will be extremely difficult to successfully implement if all players are intended to contribute equally to a chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T15:18:35-08:00","id":1059779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=1059774#post1059774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or a simple and quite rationale acknowledgement that due to the different themes and priorities of each game line, power disparities do indeed exist, and since inter-splat crossover was not only not considered important in most of the games' design (with the apparent exception of Beast), but was arguably even counterproductive for individual lines, some crossover permutations will be extremely difficult to successfully implement if all players are intended to contribute equally to a chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, you should certainly acknowledge that. But if that's <i>all</i> you do, you're doing a disservice to the XOC readership. You should then take it to the next level and address why someone might want to do such a crossover anyway and how to make it work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T15:29:37-08:00","id":1059784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=1059779#post1059779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, you should certainly acknowledge that. But if that's <i>all</i> you do, you're doing a dis<br /> I cerservice to the XOC readership. You should then take it to the next level and address why someone might want to do such a crossover anyway and how to make it work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no objection WW offering crossover ideas and suggestions, even those seemingly difficult or near impossible to implement. I will likely not choose to partake of such a chronicle, but I certainly don't begrudge others if they want to make the attempt.<br /> <br /> I'm more concerned that the crossover ideas will amount to little more than fairly significant rules and setting changes, and with the patina of &quot;official&quot; rules, it will result in causing already cantankerous arguments about splat disparities and crossover more contentious, not less.<br /> <br /> Given the inherently limited size of the Crossover Chronicle text, I'm also dubious that there'll be enough room to adequately deal with the vast myriad of crossover issues among so many major and minor splats. Whether the topic is Mage/Hunter crossover or anything other permutation, a cursory treatment runs the distinct risk of raising more questions than it answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T15:33:26-08:00","id":1059786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=1059769#post1059769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure there will be fluff-oriented stuff in there. But my understanding is that one of the motivating factors behind XOC is to address mechanical concerns of crossovers: the sorts of things that would occasionally have found their way into nWoD books such as \u201cwhat happens when a werewolf enters the Hedge\u201d or \u201cwhat happens when a vampire experiences Disquiet\u201d. ChroD books have steered clear of such matters thus far, and it turns out that they've done so because the devs have been wanting to consolidate all such matters into a single book (or perhaps a line of books?), namely XOC.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mechanics will be in there, but it's '<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=945338#post945338\">not exclusively a rulebook.</a>'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T15:33:38-08:00","id":1059787,"title":"","content":"There's a reason the devs have described XOC as their most ambitious project to date.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T15:37:49-08:00","id":1059792,"title":"","content":"Being fair, interaction between hunters and mages doesn't need to be a direct conflict where they're pitted against one another. In such a conflict, hunters get splattered. Literally or otherwise. The Sleepwalker merit allows for meaningful interaction that doesn't run head-first into the massive difference in power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T15:45:06-08:00","id":1059796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=1059792#post1059792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being fair, interaction between hunters and mages doesn't need to be a direct conflict where they're pitted against one another. In such a conflict, hunters get splattered. Literally or otherwise. The Sleepwalker merit allows for meaningful interaction that doesn't run head-first into the massive difference in power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, it just makes it horrifyingly clear how outclassed the Hunters are. Hopefully, they learn from the experience and start practicing with sniper rifles at the range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T15:51:31-08:00","id":1059799,"title":"","content":"Except for the part where I was specifically talking about situations where hunters and mages are <i>not </i>in direct competition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T15:52:37-08:00","id":1059800,"title":"","content":"Or otherwise start seeking out ways to offset the mage's advantage. There's a whole conspiracy with an Endowment designed to give mages heartburn, for instance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T16:11:38-08:00","id":1059807,"title":"","content":"I feel like the Crossover Chronicle should try to give people who want to do Crossovers as much as they can to do it.<br /> <br /> It's not like they're selling that book to people like me, who would honestly prefer to keep crossovers to a minimum where possible. Not much point doing a Crossover Chronicle catering to those who don't like crossovers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T16:17:26-08:00","id":1059810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=1059807#post1059807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not like they're selling that book to people like me, who would honestly prefer to keep crossovers to a minimum where possible. Not much point doing a Crossover Chronicle catering to those who don't like crossovers.</div> </div> </div> </div>And fortunately there will be an option for people who don't want to do crossover games, in that they can simply not purchase the book.<br /> <br /> That's probably a better way to go about it than having chapters saying 'no crossover available.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-07-2017, 07:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T16:22:40-08:00","id":1059812,"title":"","content":"It has always been an option to not use crossover material \u2014 or any other material, for that matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T16:33:24-08:00","id":1059823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=1059800#post1059800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or otherwise start seeking out ways to offset the mage's advantage. There's a whole conspiracy with an Endowment designed to give mages heartburn, for instance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I'd prefer they give helpful tips as to how to deal with and play off of the various strengths and weaknesses the different splats already have. I don't want knock off versions of the playable supernaturals. Some weaker copies that were cut down into bite sized pieces in some futile attempt at class balance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T16:50:02-08:00","id":1059828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=1059764#post1059764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still don't quite get why so many people seem so resentful of this option.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly cause it kind of cheapens the whole &quot;regular people&quot; image of Hunters, and could end up feeling like a tax that must be paid before a Hunter character can go up against Mages. There are also people who want to be able to use Paradox and Dissonance as a weapon against Mages, though I agree with Dave that wanting to do so while still being immune to Quiessence is trying to have one's cake and eat it too.<br /> <br /> Personally, my concern with this was pretty much alleviated with the addition of the Fitful Slumber and Strained Merits, which provide me exactly the kind of tools I wanted hunters and other sleepers to be able to have to help cope with Quiessence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-07-2017, 09:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T17:25:47-08:00","id":1059835,"title":"","content":"Likewise \u2014 although I still don't see any problem with an After Action Report Tactic that doesn't restore memories but does allow the cell to piece together what actually happened, especially since a single member who develops Fitful Slumber can provide more reliable information to the cell with less effort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-07-2017, 09:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T17:32:38-08:00","id":1059841,"title":"","content":"If you wanted a fun tweak on it, you could always play with the part of the Quiescence turning memories of magic to the mundane. A Sleeper Hunter who witnesses a Mage casting a spell may forcefully contextualize the memories of the act into dark and twisted shapes that fit the narrative they have in their mind, driving them away from Awakening by rendering the idea of reaching for magic to be blasphemous, morally perverse, or in some other way unconscionable.<br /> <br /> A Thyrsus who is going about their evening, conjuring and binding a woodland spirit and making it agree to a bargain, looks to the Long Night layman watching through binoculars like a devil worshiper conjuring their evil familiar spirit to renew their pact with Satan; High Speech deforms into a demonic glossolalia that haunts their dreams. If the details aren't gruesome enough, they <i>imagine</i> them to be even worse, and those who also witnessed it become susceptible to suggestion; filling in extra details, like bloody skulls and infant sacrifices with each retelling of the tale.<br /> <br /> Not only does this mean that Hunters are a very real threat to Mages (at least in the sense that they will actively interfere with the affairs of wizards), it also introduces an extra reason why Mages who use Legacy attainments purely for the benefit of their community may still come to be think of as a monster. It has both the up- and downside that it makes the Sleeping masses unreasonable, and truly unable to interface with a Mage on a meaningful level.<br /> <br /> It also gives new meaning to the idea of Satanic Panic; the phenomenon whereby seemingly sane and normal people suddenly start making up stories of occult ritual abuse and murder.<br /> <br /> This could also just be a less-common-but-still-not-unheard-of manifestation as well; something that appears in a handful of Sleepers who affect the minds of others; the sort of people who have the Liar and Communal Sleeper merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T18:56:46-08:00","id":1059874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=1059835#post1059835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Likewise \u2014 although I still don't see any problem with an After Action Report Tactic that doesn't restore memories but does allow the cell to piece together what actually happened, especially since a single member who develops Fitful Slumber can provide more reliable information to the cell with less effort.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nor I. Luckily it's a super easy tactic to add to a home game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T21:46:51-08:00","id":1059931,"title":"","content":"Still, the greatest problem on hunting the witches is not 'do you forget it', but rather 'how to hit it'. Inspired by latest Supernatural episodes I made proposed 'witch killing bullets' that nicely bypass any Mage Armor. Or shackles that limits ability to cast ( like with constant Supernal Dispellaltion effects on them).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T22:01:02-08:00","id":1059934,"title":"","content":"Finding some way to limit or deplete their Mana usage could help with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T22:16:11-08:00","id":1059937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=1059931#post1059931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, the greatest problem on hunting the witches is not 'do you forget it', but rather 'how to hit it'. Inspired by latest Supernatural episodes I made proposed 'witch killing bullets' that nicely bypass any Mage Armor. Or shackles that limits ability to cast ( like with constant Supernal Dispellaltion effects on them).</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't really make any sense to have bullets that bypass Mage Armor when half the Mage Armors work by increasing the mages ability to dodge. Doesn't matter what kinda special shit you put in bullets if a mage isn't in said bullets path. Besides, most of a mages big fuck you abilities come in the form of spells (Looking at you Ban, Alter Direction, and Turn Momentum).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 03-08-2017, 01:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T22:46:31-08:00","id":1059950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=1059841#post1059841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you wanted a fun tweak on it, you could always play with the part of the Quiescence turning memories of magic to the mundane. A Sleeper Hunter who witnesses a Mage casting a spell may forcefully contextualize the memories of the act into dark and twisted shapes that fit the narrative they have in their mind, driving them away from Awakening by rendering the idea of reaching for magic to be blasphemous, morally perverse, or in some other way unconscionable.<br /> <br /> A Thyrsus who is going about their evening, conjuring and binding a woodland spirit and making it agree to a bargain, looks to the Long Night layman watching through binoculars like a devil worshiper conjuring their evil familiar spirit to renew their pact with Satan; High Speech deforms into a demonic glossolalia that haunts their dreams. If the details aren't gruesome enough, they <i>imagine</i> them to be even worse, and those who also witnessed it become susceptible to suggestion; filling in extra details, like bloody skulls and infant sacrifices with each retelling of the tale.<br /> <br /> Not only does this mean that Hunters are a very real threat to Mages (at least in the sense that they will actively interfere with the affairs of wizards), it also introduces an extra reason why Mages who use Legacy attainments purely for the benefit of their community may still come to be think of as a monster. It has both the up- and downside that it makes the Sleeping masses unreasonable, and truly unable to interface with a Mage on a meaningful level.<br /> <br /> It also gives new meaning to the idea of Satanic Panic; the phenomenon whereby seemingly sane and normal people suddenly start making up stories of occult ritual abuse and murder.<br /> <br /> This could also just be a less-common-but-still-not-unheard-of manifestation as well; something that appears in a handful of Sleepers who affect the minds of others; the sort of people who have the Liar and Communal Sleeper merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the best way of working in Quiescence that I've ever seen. Makes it similar to Disquiet, Lunacy, Sybaris, and Bewitchment in the sense that they all poison normal humans' minds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T22:53:51-08:00","id":1059953,"title":"","content":"The good news for hunters is that while mages collectively can do pretty much anything, an individual mage is considerably more limited: not every mage has every Arcanum, and only two Arcana are freely available. The bad news is that your typical hunter doesn't know that. Still, if your cell is only going up against one mage, it may be possible for them to figure out what he can and can't do (once they've found a way around the memory loss constraint, of course), as well as what he's likely and unlikely to do: when you've got praxes and rotes, you have a tendency to prefer them over other spells, which can lead to predictability.<br /> <br /> Figuring out how to take down a mage is something that needs to be tailored to the mage. It doesn't matter if Space-based Mage Armor lets you dodge bullets if you don't have any dots in Space. And assuming that an antagonist mage is going to be optimized against the cell strikes me as white-room thinking, and/or a form of Storyteller cheating: in the messy world of actual play, the mage's abilities will likely be shaped by other concerns than whether or not a group of Sleepers are out to assassinate him \u2014 not until he's had a close call or two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T11:57:44-08:00","id":1060207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=1059950#post1059950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the best way of working in Quiescence that I've ever seen. Makes it similar to Disquiet, Lunacy, Sybaris, and Bewitchment in the sense that they all poison normal humans' minds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool! To be honest, I always liked playing with the Lie as something that works to prevent Awakening first and foremost, in whatever form that takes. Forgetting is one way, but if it can be shifted into another that causes a stronger and more aggressive rejection of magic, why not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T00:02:07-08:00","id":1060433,"title":"","content":"Isn't that exactly what I was proposing in the opening post?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T05:37:47-08:00","id":1060482,"title":"","content":"Looks like it is. Guess that's what happens when you come into things midway, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T12:23:13-08:00","id":1060974,"title":"","content":"Another possible compromise: Mage 2E mentions that direct exposure to the Lie can sometimes cause an Awakening. Mage 2e <i>also</i> says that anything that can trigger Awakening could, instead, result in a Sleeper becoming a Sleepwalker. Put it all together and you get the idea that exposure to magic or the Abyss can (sometimes, unpredictably) turn Sleepers into Sleepwalkers.<br /> <br /> So run your Sleeping hunters through a mindfuck scenario where they go up against a magical or Abyssal threat, to give them a taste of how terrifying Supernal magic can be. Then let them develop the Sleepwalker merit as a result of their experiences, giving them a chance to fight back. Rather than an arbitrary bonus, Sleepwalker status becomes something they've <i>earned,</i> by going up against Things Man Was Not Meant to Know and surviving.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/40-dspaul","name":"DSPaul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T12:33:09-08:00","id":1060978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DSPaul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=1060974#post1060974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another possible compromise: Mage 2E mentions that direct exposure to the Lie can sometimes cause an Awakening. Mage 2e <i>also</i> says that anything that can trigger Awakening could, instead, result in a Sleeper becoming a Sleepwalker. Put it all together and you get the idea that exposure to magic or the Abyss can (sometimes, unpredictably) turn Sleepers into Sleepwalkers.<br /> <br /> So run your Sleeping hunters through a mindfuck scenario where they go up against a magical or Abyssal threat, to give them a taste of how terrifying Supernal magic can be. Then let them develop the Sleepwalker merit as a result of their experiences, giving them a chance to fight back. Rather than an arbitrary bonus, Sleepwalker status becomes something they've <i>earned,</i> by going up against Things Man Was Not Meant to Know and surviving.</div> </div> </div> </div>Straight from the corebook: <br /> &quot;Fitful Slumber ( \u2022 )<br /> Prerequisites: The character has suffered three or more <br /> breaking points due to exposure to the Supernal or Abyss and <br /> is now considered a Sleepwalker, even if he did not start the <br /> game that way. <br /> Effect: Because of the regular abuse, your character is able to <br /> resist breaking points triggered by all things Abyssal or Supernal <br /> with a +2 bonus. &quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T22:34:53-08:00","id":1061139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DSPaul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=1060974#post1060974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another possible compromise: Mage 2E mentions that direct exposure to the Lie can sometimes cause an Awakening. Mage 2e <i>also</i> says that anything that can trigger Awakening could, instead, result in a Sleeper becoming a Sleepwalker. Put it all together and you get the idea that exposure to magic or the Abyss can (sometimes, unpredictably) turn Sleepers into Sleepwalkers.<br /> <br /> So run your Sleeping hunters through a mindfuck scenario where they go up against a magical or Abyssal threat, to give them a taste of how terrifying Supernal magic can be. Then let them develop the Sleepwalker merit as a result of their experiences, giving them a chance to fight back. Rather than an arbitrary bonus, Sleepwalker status becomes something they've <i>earned,</i> by going up against Things Man Was Not Meant to Know and surviving.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you're describing the Fitful Slumber Merit, which I called out as one of the Merits that gives Sleepers the kind of tools I want them to have access to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T23:49:26-08:00","id":1061147,"title":"","content":"I love that merit. We based a whole unfortunate &quot;kinda illegal but everyone thinks everyone do it so no one try to do something about it&quot; practice on it. In our games, Mage population is much smaller than associated Sleeper Sleepwalker &quot;pyramid&quot; under them, and a lot of estabilished Mages wraps themselves in Sleeper Cults [the fact that we houserule Sleeping Curse to modify memories of Magic not to &quot;mundane stuff&quot; but to &quot;most believable NON SUPERNAL explanation for the victim, including lower case magic, supernatural, ESP, UFO, etc] where they first carefully shape their victims worldview [so the Curse will rationalize Magic for them in the &quot;wanted&quot; way] and then procedurally abuse Integrity of the few chosen ones in hope they will get the Fitful Slumber Merit.<br /> <br /> It also makes hunters, police and other investigators much less ignorant; not unignorant enough to TRULY grasp the beauty of Magic, but unignorant enough to perceive how dangerous it is. <br /> <br /> I've always felt it's ok for non Mages to know about Mages, as long as they cannot grasp Supernal for what it is. Makes Mage even more tragic than &quot;they just rationalize it to gas leaks&quot; imho, especially because you can try to fool yourself into thinking that maaaaaaaaaaaaybe they are one breaking point away from getting it. Integrity Bombing your own family and then despairing that they are almost getting it, but that almost is in the worst MISSING THE POINT way anyone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T00:28:12-08:00","id":1061152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=1061147#post1061147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love that merit. We based a whole unfortunate &quot;kinda illegal but everyone thinks everyone do it so no one try to do something about it&quot; practice on it. In our games, Mage population is much smaller than associated Sleeper Sleepwalker &quot;pyramid&quot; under them, and a lot of estabilished Mages wraps themselves in Sleeper Cults [the fact that we houserule Sleeping Curse to modify memories of Magic not to &quot;mundane stuff&quot; but to &quot;most believable NON SUPERNAL explanation for the victim, including lower case magic, supernatural, ESP, UFO, etc] where they first carefully shape their victims worldview [so the Curse will rationalize Magic for them in the &quot;wanted&quot; way] and then procedurally abuse Integrity of the few chosen ones in hope they will get the Fitful Slumber Merit.<br /> <br /> It also makes hunters, police and other investigators much less ignorant; not unignorant enough to TRULY grasp the beauty of Magic, but unignorant enough to perceive how dangerous it is.<br /> <br /> I've always felt it's ok for non Mages to know about Mages, as long as they cannot grasp Supernal for what it is. Makes Mage even more tragic than &quot;they just rationalize it to gas leaks&quot; imho, especially because you can try to fool yourself into thinking that maaaaaaaaaaaaybe they are one breaking point away from getting it. Integrity Bombing your own family and then despairing that they are almost getting it, but that almost is in the worst MISSING THE POINT way anyone?</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely prefer the &quot;'mundane' means non-Supernal, not non-supernatural&quot; interpretation for just that reason. It also makes it <i>more</i> likely for Hunters and such to try and hunt down Mages, as others have mentioned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T04:06:33-08:00","id":1061193,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately, mundane means non-supernatural, not just non-Supernal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T04:34:21-08:00","id":1061197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=1061147#post1061147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love that merit. We based a whole unfortunate &quot;kinda illegal but everyone thinks everyone do it so no one try to do something about it&quot; practice on it. In our games, Mage population is much smaller than associated Sleeper Sleepwalker &quot;pyramid&quot; under them, and a lot of estabilished Mages wraps themselves in Sleeper Cults [the fact that we houserule Sleeping Curse to modify memories of Magic not to &quot;mundane stuff&quot; but to &quot;most believable NON SUPERNAL explanation for the victim, including lower case magic, supernatural, ESP, UFO, etc] where they first carefully shape their victims worldview [so the Curse will rationalize Magic for them in the &quot;wanted&quot; way] and then procedurally abuse Integrity of the few chosen ones in hope they will get the Fitful Slumber Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like that idea. You can effectively overawe sleepers and bend them to your will but it requires reinforcing the Lie. That's a pretty great dilemma right there. Also it potentially gives the Seers a big advantage in that they generally aren't going to be too bothered by messing with the Lie too much (as long as the world isn't pulled into the Abyss, we're good).<br /> <br /> One other thing to consider is that that seems a great way to create Banishers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T11:58:25-08:00","id":1061302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=1061193#post1061193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately, mundane means non-supernatural, not just non-Supernal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense. Given how diverse non-Supernal supernatural phenomena are, <i>not</i> restricting it to exclude all sorts of supernatural would pretty much defang Quiescence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T12:23:03-08:00","id":1061310,"title":"","content":"And also especially as the Lie seems to be an anti-awakening force as much as it as an anti-awakened force, and awakenings seem to at times be triggered by sleepers attempting to understand the supernatural. Making their supernal magic experiences entirely mundane suppresses their desire to learn about something beyond the normal world they think they live in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T12:36:44-08:00","id":1061315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=1061302#post1061302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Makes sense. Given how diverse non-Supernal supernatural phenomena are, <i>not</i> restricting it to exclude all sorts of supernatural would pretty much defang Quiescence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure they meant it this way, but at the time I assumed due to the examples that WHW meant 'supernatural' in the mundane sense. Like, whilst in the CoD setting real supernatural beings do exist, there's presumably still the same real world supernatural pop culture that people believe in the real world.<br /> <br /> You're not mistaking Supernal magic for something that's real, you're mistaking it for something that's wrong.<br /> <br /> I'm kinda thinking of the cabal in Banishers which believes magi are aliens. They're not mistaking magi for real aliens that they've seen. They're taking bits of UFO culture and projecting it onto the Awakened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T13:25:53-08:00","id":1061322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=1061147#post1061147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love that merit. We based a whole unfortunate &amp;quot;kinda illegal but everyone thinks everyone do it so no one try to do something about it&amp;quot; practice on it. In our games, Mage population is much smaller than associated Sleeper Sleepwalker &amp;quot;pyramid&amp;quot; under them, and a lot of estabilished Mages wraps themselves in Sleeper Cults [the fact that we houserule Sleeping Curse to modify memories of Magic not to &amp;quot;mundane stuff&amp;quot; but to &amp;quot;most believable NON SUPERNAL explanation for the victim, including lower case magic, supernatural, ESP, UFO, etc] where they first carefully shape their victims worldview [so the Curse will rationalize Magic for them in the &amp;quot;wanted&amp;quot; way] and then procedurally abuse Integrity of the few chosen ones in hope they will get the Fitful Slumber Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just want to say, pretty much everything I hear about your games makes them sound incredibly fun to play in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T15:44:51-08:00","id":1061366,"title":"","content":"In a crossover mage vs hunter game, I feel like the conspiracies might be influenced by mage orders similar to how it's alluded that vampires influence TFV against other vampires.<br /> <br /> In my opinion, hunters are the perfect tool to teach a mage about wisdom and utilizing their magic dangerously. Because of that, I feel like the guardians of the veil (maybe?) might take a particular interest in utilizing a group of hunters - not to kill a mage or group of mages, but to educate them on how that lack of wisdom can create issues. So if you wanted to utilize hunters as an antagonist to mage, it may be a good trick to have them have a 'patron' to make them more effective. I don't know that I'd see them as a lethal threat, but part of mage is the hubris of them - just because your a god doesn't mean you'll survive a bullet to the brain, and that's why it makes an effective hubris/wisdom lesson.<br /> <br /> If the other direction was taken - hunters versus mages - the same philosophy could apply if the mage is particularly powerful. If they aren't, then a group of hunters might be a threat to a mage though probably not a full cabal - so maybe have them against one mage or two mages, but not a whole group of them; My thoughts there are... well, an order or consilium isn't going to see hunters as a 'threat' so they won't send the entire cities' mage groups against them, and it may well be written off if that mage is killed as the mages own fault, because of how little a threat hunters are assumed to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}